{
  "raw": {
    "https://belmont.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/10/home/requisition/4983?c=belmont": {
      "title": "Armed Security Officer",
      "description": "Armed Security Officer | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Armed Security Officer United States | req4983 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/20/2026 Back to Search Armed Security Officer We are now accepting applications for a qualified Armed Security Officer at Belmont University. Employment Type Staff Internal Job Category Non-Exempt (Staff) Full-Time Department Campus Security Hours 40 Primary Duties and Responsibilities: The Armed Security Officer position exists to patrol the campus, protect property, and respond to emergency situations and requests for assistance. This position is eligible to receive a shift differential. This position offers paid training. Belmont's Office of Campus Security is here around the clock — 24 hours a day, 7 days a week, 365 days a year — to keep our community safe. Our team of more than 40 trained officers patrols campus, responds to emergencies and works alongside students, faculty and staff to maintain a safe and welcoming environment for everyone who calls Belmont home. Every OCS officer is trained to respond to medical, criminal and weather-related emergencies. Maintain a positive and courteous demeanor at all times; practice open dialogue and understanding, and communicate with others in an honest, professional, and respectful manner. Interact, provide and exchange information with students, employees and guests; develops a rapport with members of the university community and surrounding areas; participate in community relations activities. Demonstrate a high level of awareness, good judgment, and critical thinking skills in all aspects of the position. Conduct pro-active, high visibility patrol to prevent theft, vandalism, or other criminal offenses and to identify opportunities to engage and provide service to the campus community and visitors. Observe for and investigate unusual or suspicious circumstances, inappropriate use of University facilities or property. Remain attentive for, report, and follow up on potential security concerns and hazards such as lighting, access control, alarm systems, fire safety, and other concerns that may affect the safety or effective operation of the University. Enforce parking regulations on campus by ticketing, immobilizing, and towing as appropriate. Perform general security duties including escorts, jump starts, vehicle accesses, response to fire/duress/burglar alarms, medical/psychological emergencies, and calls for service; building checks, accesses, lock ups, and preliminary investigation of incidents occurring on campus. May provide direction to contract security such as CSC and Apex at special events. May respond to and assist with traffic accidents on or in close proximity to campus until the arrival of proper authorities. May respond to provide assistance and service to members of the BU community in proximity to campus as needed. Act as first responder to incidents and emergencies. Maintains a working knowledge of the University’s Emergency Management Plan; establishes command and implements ICS on any significant crime, emergency, or other serious incident, in accordance with NIMS / ICS training and the Belmont emergency management plan. May perform first aid and assist police, fire, EMS, and other responders. Acts as liaison with local law enforcement agencies. Participates in debriefs and critiques to ensure continuous improvement. Ensure all needed notifications have been made in timely fashion, that accurate information has been communicated, and that information has been properly documented via incidents via incident reports, maintenance requests, field interview cards, jump start forms, vehicle assistance forms, affidavits of complaint, and student misconduct forms. May assist with orienting new hires to duties and responsibilities. May present on security-related topics for the campus community as well as presenting in-service training for officers. Other duties as assigned. Required Qualifications : Belmont University seeks to attract and retain highly qualified faculty and staff who will support our mission and vision. As a Christ-centered and student-focused community, we aim to: Form diverse leaders of character; Equip people to solve the world’s complex problems through teaching, research and service; And be radical champions for helping people and communities flourish. Must be trained in, or have the ability to complete training in, critical incident management including the Incident Command System, the National Incident Management System, and the IPMBA Bicycle Certification Program. Self-restraint in challenging situations Excellent oral and written communication skills, including the ability to articulate observations and explain actions, and to write clear and concise reports, as well as make presentations to campus groups Active listening skills and an ability to understand and follow written and verbal instructions An ability to relate to and gain the confidence and cooperation of the university community, an ability to deal tactfully and effectively with a wide variety of people and act calmly and rationally in an emergency An ability to work with minimal supervision, handle multiple priorities, and maintain confidentiality An ability to operate computer equipment and a two-way radio. An ability to take ownership and actively seek chances to assist others. An ability to assess/effectively manage crises. Experience working in a fast-paced environment and the ability to respond to high-pressure situations. Ability to thrive in an environment of hard work. An ability to work effectively with a wide range of constituencies in a diverse community. Required Education A high school diploma or equivalency is required. A Bachelor's Degree in Criminal Justice, Business, or Law Enforcement is preferred. Required Experience Be a registered armed security guard in the State of Tennessee or be able to qualify. Be at least 21 years of age and possess a valid ID. Be a citizen, or resident alien, of the United States. Be legally mentally competent. Be of good moral character. Be free of habitual drunkenness or narcotics addiction or dependence. Must be able to pass an FBI/TBI-based background check. The State of Tennessee requires sentences/probation to be completed at least 5 years prior. Have no disability which would prevent performance of duties. Employees work outdoors and may not be protected from weather conditions. Position includes a variety of physical conditions, such as proximity to moving mechanical parts of machinery or tools used to perform work, moving vehicles, electrical current, working on scaffolding and high places, or exposure to chemicals. Conditions that affect the respiratory system, such as fumes, odors, dusts, mists, gases, or poor ventilation. This position requires sitting, repetitive hand motion, hearing, listening, talking, standing, walking, bending, stooping, climbing stairs/ladders, kneeling/squatting, crouching, crawling, reaching overhead, pulling, pushing, shoveling, frequently lifting up to 20 pounds, occasionally lifting up to 50 pounds, and occasionally lifting over 50 pounds. Must meet the state-regulated training requirements. A minimum of three years’ experience demonstrating reliability and accountability, good judgment, good customer service skills, discretion, decision-making and problem-solving abilities, teamwork and excellent interpersonal skills is required. Related experience in an institution of higher education is preferred. First Aid and CPR certification and a demonstrated ability to work in a multi-cultural setting is also preferred. The selected candidate will be required to complete a background check satisfactory to the University. Belmont University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Apply Now Share Save Job Belmont University is a Christ-centered community. The University faculty, administration, and staff uphold Jesus as the Christ and as the measure for all things. As a community seeking to uphold Christian standards of morality, ethics, and conduct, Belmont University holds high expectations of each person who chooses to join the community. In compliance with federal law, including provisions of Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Titles VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, the Age Discrimination in Employment Act and Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973/the Americans with Disabilities Act, Belmont University does not discriminate on the basis of race, sex, color, national or ethnic origin, age, disability, military service, or sexual orientation in its administration of education policies, programs or activities; its admissions policies; or employment. Consistent with applicable civil rights law, the University primarily hires employees of the Christian faith who are committed to support the mission of the University. The University has appointed the Chief Human Resources Officer/Deputy Title IX Coordinator to serve as coordinator of non-discrimination compliance for staff and faculty. The Director of Institutional Equity and Compliance and Title IX Coordinator serves as coordinator of compliance for Title IX (sex discrimination) issues and questions for students. Click here to learn more. *In accordance with accrediting standards for its professional education programs in law and medicine, the University does not apply religious criteria in hiring employees within those programs. All employees hired by the University, regardless of religious faith, shall be committed to Belmont’s Christ-centered, student-focused mission. Belmont's Office of Human Resources will conduct ongoing evaluations of the means by which candidates for employment are sought, to the end that the pool of candidates will include qualified women, minorities, veterans and disabled individuals. Belmont University is an equal opportunity employer under all applicable civil rights laws."
    },
    "https://belmont.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/10/home/requisition/4982?c=belmont": {
      "title": "Dean, Belmont University Mike Curb College of Entertainment & Music Business",
      "description": "Dean, Belmont University Mike Curb College of Entertainment & Music Business | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Dean, Belmont University Mike Curb College of Entertainment & Music Business United States | req4982 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/19/2026 Back to Search Dean, Belmont University Mike Curb College of Entertainment & Music Business We are now accepting applications for a qualified Dean, Belmont University Mike Curb College of Entertainment & Music Business at Belmont University. Employment Type Staff Internal Job Category Exempt (Staff) Full-Time Department College Entertain & Music Bus Hours Primary Duties and Responsibilities: Belmont University is seeking a dynamic visionary\nleader, scholar, educator, and practitioner to build upon the extraordinary\nsuccess of the Belmont University College of Entertainment and Music Business,\nand lead its outstanding faculty, staff, students, alumni, and partners into\nthe future. Belmont University (https://www.belmont.edu/) is a private, Christ-centered university focusing on\nacademic excellence and whole person formation. Belmont is an ecumenical\nChristian institution located in the heart of Nashville, one of the fastest\ngrowing and most culturally rich cities in the country. Serving nearly 9,000\nstudents from every state, more than 35 countries, and a diversity of faith\ntraditions, Belmont University is the second largest private university in\nTennessee. The Mike Curb College of\nEntertainment & Music Business (CEMB) (https://www.belmont.edu/curb/about/) located on Nashville’s iconic Music Row, is a globally recognized leader\nin entertainment and music business education, preparing the next generation of\nindustry leaders across music, media, film, television, publishing, sports and\nemerging entertainment sectors. Since its roots in Belmont’s pioneering music\nbusiness program established in 1973 and its formal designation as the Mike\nCurb College in 2003, CEMB has built an exceptional reputation for academic\nexcellence, industry engagement and career-ready learning. With a distinguished\nfaculty that includes scholars, entrepreneurs, songwriters, producers and\nindustry professionals, CEMB offers innovative undergraduate and graduate\nprograms that connect theory with practice and position students to launch\nimpactful careers from day one. Guided by its mission to shape culture through\nentertainment education that fosters wisdom, character and community, CEMB\nseeks a visionary dean who will advance its global leadership, strengthen\nindustry partnerships, promote academic innovation and inspire a community\ndedicated to preparing leaders of character who will shape the future of the\nentertainment industry. Reporting directly to\nthe Provost & Executive Vice President for Academic Excellence, the Dean of\nthe College of Entertainment & Music Business (CEMB) will serve as the\nacademic and organizational leader of Belmont University’s highly regarded and\nlargest college, and will demonstrate exceptional character, creativity, and\ninnovation in line with the University’s key principles. Stakeholders have\nidentified vision, integrity, transparency, trustworthiness, authenticity, visibility,\nan even temperament, and possessing a student-focus as desired characteristics\nof the next Dean. The Dean will be an exemplary representative of and\nrelentless advocate for CEMB and Belmont University. The\nDean will communicate Belmont’s mission to external stakeholders; build\nphilanthropic support among alumni, parents, donors, and partners; and bring a\ncollaborative, relational leadership style to this work. Success in this role will require the ability to lead\nwithin a complex organization, understand future trends in the entertainment industry and higher\neducation, and\nremain committed to Belmont’s Christ-centered, student-focused mission. The Dean will oversee CEMB’s academic degrees which consist of: Undergraduate Programs (https://www.belmont.edu/curb/programs.html): Music Business Songwriting Animation & Media Arts Cinema & Television Studies Film & Television Writing Media Production Motion Picture Production Journalism Media & Entertainment Industries Publishing Audio Engineering Technology Sports Administration Graduate Programs (https://www.belmont.edu/curb/programs.html): Audio Engineering Media & Entertainment Industries Sports Administration In addition to providing academic leadership\nand strategic direction for CEMB, the Dean will cultivate partnerships that create relevant, experiential student learning opportunities across campus and throughout\nthe entertainment and music business industries. The Dean will steward CEMB’s resources through effective financial\nmanagement, thoughtful deployment of personnel, and\npurposeful fundraising\nthat supports CEMB’s mission and strategic priorities. The next Dean will have a strong record of successful leadership, demonstrated skill as an effective and collaborative executive,\nand be gifted in relationship building, fund raising, and the capacity to foster an entrepreneurial spirit among the CEMB\nteam. The Dean must\nalso possess a robust capacity to manage a complex organization, demonstrate a\nbroad intellectual orientation and appreciation for future trends impacting\nhigher education, and have a passion for the transformational power of higher\neducation.  It is also critical that\nregardless of the Dean’s religious faith, they will have the capacity to lead\nCEMB on Belmont University’s Christ-centered, student-focused mission. Belmont College of Entertainment\nand Music Business reserves the right to exercise a preference for those\ncandidates who support the goals and mission of the University. You may read\nBelmont’s Non-Discrimination statement at https://www.belmont.edu/notices/nondiscrimination.html . Other Key Responsibilities of the Dean: Serve as the chief academic and administrative officer for the College, fostering a culture of teamwork and collaboration. Cultivate and steward relationships with alumni, corporate sponsors, donors, industry partners, and the professional community. Be a recognized leader within entertainment, media, sports, and creative industries in order to meet fundraising and engagement objectives in partnership with the Office of Development. Work collaboratively with university marketing and communications and the Office of the President around strategic branding opportunities. Identify and foster opportunities for collaboration across the various Colleges within Belmont University. Provide leadership and supervision for CEMB associate deans, assistant deans, department chairs, faculty, and staff, and provide support and guidance for organizational, curricular, and administrative work related to the CEMB. Oversee the student educational experience, including student learning, formation, support, retention, and success. Lead student recruitment and enrollment growth strategies for CEMB in partnership with university enrollment, marketing, and admissions teams. Advance continuous improvement across academic initiatives, with attention to teaching, scholarship, student support, and service. Lead the programmatic accreditation processes within the college, ensuring compliance with relevant accrediting bodies. Commit to continual improvement of current and future curricula with attentiveness to new program creation,innovation, or emerging industry opportunities. Collaborate with other deans, university administrators, and faculty members to advance interdisciplinary initiatives, research collaborations, and shared educational resources. Participate in university-wide structures, committees and initiatives as necessary, contributing to the overall strategic direction of the university. Manage CEMB’s financial resources and budget responsibly in alignment with strategic priorities. Collaborate with the university administration to allocate resources efficiently, seek external funding opportunities, and make strategic investments in faculty, staff, and infrastructure. Recruit, hire, and evaluate exceptional faculty members in accordance with University policies and CEMB practices. Mentor and support faculty through professional development opportunities that foster excellence, collaboration, and innovation. Perform other duties as assigned and directed by the President or Provost & Executive Vice-President for Academic Excellence. Preferred Qualifications : Belmont University seeks to attract and retain highly qualified faculty and staff who will support our mission and vision. As a Christ-centered and student-focused community, we aim to: Form diverse leaders of character; Equip people to solve the world’s complex problems through teaching, research and service; And be radical champions for helping people and communities flourish. Capacity to lead a unit that embodies Belmont University’s Christ-centered institutional mission Evidence of successful leadership experience in an academic and/or professional environment. Demonstrated success in fundraising, donor cultivation, and external engagement. Demonstrated aptitude in developing, articulating, and implementing a strategic direction within a complex institution. Background, experience, and qualifications that would merit appointment to the faculty at the rank of full professor with tenure. An appreciation of Belmont University - its past, present, and future. Long-standing dedication to academic excellence, scholarship, and learning. Demonstrated leadership in promoting hope, unity and belonging among staff, faculty, and students. Uncompromising personal and professional integrity. Outstanding communication and interpersonal skills. Strong financial and resource management skills with the ability to make strategic budget decisions. Ability to listen to divergent views while building consensus and collegiality. Required Education Advanced or terminal degree preferred. Required Experience At least five years of progressively increasing responsibility and leadership; Experience in the practice of music business or entertainment or other professions that demonstrate professional achievement. The selected candidate will be required to complete a background check satisfactory to the University. Belmont University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Apply Now Share Save Job Belmont University is a Christ-centered community. The University faculty, administration, and staff uphold Jesus as the Christ and as the measure for all things. As a community seeking to uphold Christian standards of morality, ethics, and conduct, Belmont University holds high expectations of each person who chooses to join the community. In compliance with federal law, including provisions of Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Titles VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, the Age Discrimination in Employment Act and Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973/the Americans with Disabilities Act, Belmont University does not discriminate on the basis of race, sex, color, national or ethnic origin, age, disability, military service, or sexual orientation in its administration of education policies, programs or activities; its admissions policies; or employment. Consistent with applicable civil rights law, the University primarily hires employees of the Christian faith who are committed to support the mission of the University. The University has appointed the Chief Human Resources Officer/Deputy Title IX Coordinator to serve as coordinator of non-discrimination compliance for staff and faculty. The Director of Institutional Equity and Compliance and Title IX Coordinator serves as coordinator of compliance for Title IX (sex discrimination) issues and questions for students. Click here to learn more. *In accordance with accrediting standards for its professional education programs in law and medicine, the University does not apply religious criteria in hiring employees within those programs. All employees hired by the University, regardless of religious faith, shall be committed to Belmont’s Christ-centered, student-focused mission. Belmont's Office of Human Resources will conduct ongoing evaluations of the means by which candidates for employment are sought, to the end that the pool of candidates will include qualified women, minorities, veterans and disabled individuals. Belmont University is an equal opportunity employer under all applicable civil rights laws."
    },
    "https://belmont.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/10/home/requisition/362?c=belmont": {
      "title": "Office of Community & Government Relations - Communications Assistant",
      "description": "Office of Community & Government Relations - Communications Assistant | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Office of Community & Government Relations - Communications Assistant United States | 8888 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/16/2026 Back to Search Office of Community & Government Relations - Communications Assistant Employment Type Student Employee Hourly Rate $11.00 Special Note: All students are required to read the BU Student Employment Policy prior to submitting an application. All Federal Work-Study students should read the program rules and regulations located at http://www.belmont.edu/sfs/employment/fws.html Primary Duties and Responsibilities The student in this position will assist Office of Community and Government Relations in strengthening the partnership with Metropolitan Board of Parks and Recreation and Easley Center by helping to market and do public relations that will improve Parks and Recreation’s outreach for Parks’ programs designed to meet the changing needs of the Edgehill community. Help to plan and execute tailored communications vehicles, including social media, to communicate with constituents and partners in the Edgehill/Rose Park area for Metro Parks Do data entry as necessary. Meet with Metro Parks and Easley Center/Rose Park staff and develop relationships with Belmont's Edgehill neighborhood partners. May attend neighborhood meetings. May facilitate or work with Edgehill youth to produce communications designed to promote programs at Easley Center/Rose Park. Required Qualifications Excellent grammar Spelling & punctuation Knowledge of regulations governing publication of written material Organizational skills Working knowledge of computer software programs used to write and edit various materials Proofreading and editing skills Ability to write and speak clearly and effectively Ability to establish relationships Use of Social Media Work on deadline Confidentiality Have or use transportation to work off Belmont campus. Required Education Must be enrolled as a current student at Belmont. Required Experience Paid or volunteer work on print or electronic newspaper, blogs, YouTubes, social media for high school, college, church, non-profit, etc. Apply Now Share Save Job Belmont University is a Christ-centered community. The University faculty, administration, and staff uphold Jesus as the Christ and as the measure for all things. As a community seeking to uphold Christian standards of morality, ethics, and conduct, Belmont University holds high expectations of each person who chooses to join the community. In compliance with federal law, including provisions of Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Titles VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, the Age Discrimination in Employment Act and Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973/the Americans with Disabilities Act, Belmont University does not discriminate on the basis of race, sex, color, national or ethnic origin, age, disability, military service, or sexual orientation in its administration of education policies, programs or activities; its admissions policies; or employment. Consistent with applicable civil rights law, the University primarily hires employees of the Christian faith who are committed to support the mission of the University. The University has appointed the Chief Human Resources Officer/Deputy Title IX Coordinator to serve as coordinator of non-discrimination compliance for staff and faculty. The Director of Institutional Equity and Compliance and Title IX Coordinator serves as coordinator of compliance for Title IX (sex discrimination) issues and questions for students. Click here to learn more. *In accordance with accrediting standards for its professional education programs in law and medicine, the University does not apply religious criteria in hiring employees within those programs. All employees hired by the University, regardless of religious faith, shall be committed to Belmont’s Christ-centered, student-focused mission. Belmont's Office of Human Resources will conduct ongoing evaluations of the means by which candidates for employment are sought, to the end that the pool of candidates will include qualified women, minorities, veterans and disabled individuals. Belmont University is an equal opportunity employer under all applicable civil rights laws."
