    "https://belmont.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/10/home/requisition/4980?c=belmont": {
      "title": "Grant Funded--PRN Mobile Clinic Driver",
      "description": "Grant Funded--PRN Mobile Clinic Driver | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Grant Funded--PRN Mobile Clinic Driver United States | req4980 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/14/2026 Back to Search Grant Funded--PRN Mobile Clinic Driver We are now accepting applications for a qualified Grant Funded--PRN Mobile Clinic Driver at Belmont University. Employment Type Staff Internal Job Category Non-Exempt (Staff) Part-Time Department Public Health Hours Primary Duties and Responsibilities: We are seeking Mobile Clinic Drivers to serve as part of the Flourish Mobile Health Clinic team on an as-needed basis. This position provides backup coverage when a regular mobile clinic driver is unavailable due to illness, vacation, or other circumstances. This position may be needed approximately 5-10 times per year, with shifts ranging from a single day to several days depending on the coverage needed. The driver will safely operate the mobile truck and trailer (clinic), transport supplies, equipment, and medications, and assist with setup, breakdown, and general clinic operations. This person will also assist Flourish staff and engage respectfully and compassionately with individuals affected by substance use disorders, homelessness, and other barriers to healthcare. Primary position responsibilities: Safely operate and drive the Flourish mobile clinic and/or outreach vehicle to scheduled community locations. Assist with setting up and breaking down the mobile clinic and ensuring the vehicle is clean, organized, stocked, and ready for service. Help create a welcoming, safe, and nonjudgmental environment for individuals accessing Flourish services. The above statements describe the job’s essential responsibilities and requirements.  They are not an exhaustive list of the duties that may be assigned to job incumbents. This position is funded in whole or in part by a grant. Employment is subject to the continued availability of grant funding and does not imply a guarantee of employment beyond the grant period. Required Qualifications : Belmont University seeks to attract and retain highly qualified faculty and staff who will support our mission and vision. As a Christ-centered and student-focused community, we aim to: Form diverse leaders of character; Equip people to solve the world’s complex problems through teaching, research and service; And be radical champions for helping people and communities flourish. Analytical Thinking: Ability to identify issues, obtain relevant information, relate and compare data from different sources, and identify alternative solutions. Experience working in a fast-paced environment and the ability to respond to high-pressure situations. Ability to thrive in an environment of hard work. Ability to work effectively with a wide range of constituencies in a diverse community. Required Education High school diploma or GED required. Class A or B CDL or Previously Held Class A or B CDL highly preferred. Required Experience 4-6 years experience operating large vehicles and towing trailers, including semi-trucks, semi-trailers, RVs, boats, or similar vehicles is required. 10-15 years experience is preferred. The selected candidate will be required to complete a background check satisfactory to the University. Belmont University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Apply Now Share Save Job Belmont University is a Christ-centered community. The University faculty, administration, and staff uphold Jesus as the Christ and as the measure for all things. As a community seeking to uphold Christian standards of morality, ethics, and conduct, Belmont University holds high expectations of each person who chooses to join the community. In compliance with federal law, including provisions of Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Titles VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, the Age Discrimination in Employment Act and Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973/the Americans with Disabilities Act, Belmont University does not discriminate on the basis of race, sex, color, national or ethnic origin, age, disability, military service, or sexual orientation in its administration of education policies, programs or activities; its admissions policies; or employment. Consistent with applicable civil rights law, the University primarily hires employees of the Christian faith who are committed to support the mission of the University. The University has appointed the Chief Human Resources Officer/Deputy Title IX Coordinator to serve as coordinator of non-discrimination compliance for staff and faculty. The Director of Institutional Equity and Compliance and Title IX Coordinator serves as coordinator of compliance for Title IX (sex discrimination) issues and questions for students. Click here to learn more. *In accordance with accrediting standards for its professional education programs in law and medicine, the University does not apply religious criteria in hiring employees within those programs. All employees hired by the University, regardless of religious faith, shall be committed to Belmont’s Christ-centered, student-focused mission. Belmont's Office of Human Resources will conduct ongoing evaluations of the means by which candidates for employment are sought, to the end that the pool of candidates will include qualified women, minorities, veterans and disabled individuals. Belmont University is an equal opportunity employer under all applicable civil rights laws."
    },
    "https://belmont.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/10/home/requisition/4979?c=belmont": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Nursing",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Nursing | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Assistant/Associate Professor of Nursing United States | req4979 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/14/2026 Back to Search Assistant/Associate Professor of Nursing We are now accepting applications for a qualified Assistant/Associate Professor of Nursing at Belmont University. Employment Type Faculty Internal Job Category Tenure Track (Faculty) Full-Time Department College of Nursing Hours N/A Primary Duties and Responsibilities: The College of Nursing at Belmont University is seeking applications for 10-month tenure-track faculty positions at the rank of Assistant/Associate Professor beginning August 1st, 2027. Faculty hired for these positions will be expected to engage in classroom, clinical, lab, and/or simulation. While the primary need is in undergraduate nursing programs, there may be opportunities/requirements to teach in the graduate program for qualified candidates with specific experience and expertise. Preference will be given to candidates with experience in behavioral health, public health nursing, nursing informatics, and/or a demonstrated record of leadership and innovation in nursing science. A doctorate degree (DNP, PhD.) in nursing and academic experience is strongly preferred. Additional responsibilities include academic advising, student mentoring, scholarly activity, interprofessional engagement, and college and university service. Additional responsibilities include: Advise and mentor students in research and other class-related projects. Engage in activities to support the mission and vision of Belmont University and the college in which you teach. Participate in departmental and university committee work. Engage in scholarly activity and professional development. Advise students in course selection and degree completion. Participate in a local church and the community. Abide by all relevant university and/or department procedures and policies. Maintain regular on-campus office hours. The above statements describe the job’s essential responsibilities and requirements. They are not an exhaustive list of the duties that may be assigned to job incumbents. Additional Information As all Belmont undergraduates complete an innovative general education program with significant interdisciplinary components, Belmont University is particularly seeking applicants who can demonstrate the interest and ability to work collaboratively in course design and to teach interdisciplinary and topical courses in this program. For additional information about the position and to complete the online application, candidates are directed to https://jobs.belmont.edu. An electronic version of a Cover Letter, Curriculum Vitae/Resume, and Response to Belmont’s Aspirational Aim must be attached to complete the online application. During the application process, applicants will be asked to attach a cover letter, Curriculum Vita/Resume and prepare a one-page essay, 300-400 words, describing how your core beliefs and practices inform your support of our Christ-Centered mission and influence your teaching, research, and service philosophy. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until February 1st, 2027. The selected candidate for this position must complete a background check satisfactory to the University. Located near the heart of thriving Nashville, Tennessee, Belmont University consists of nearly 9,000 students who come from every state and 33 countries. The University is nationally recognized for its innovative approach and commitment to undergraduate teaching. As a Christ-centered, student-focused community, Belmont’s mission is to develop diverse leaders of character, wisdom and a transformational mindset. With more than 130 areas of undergraduate study, 29 master’s programs and eight doctoral degrees, Belmont University aims to be the leading Christ-centered university in the world, producing leaders who will radically champion the pursuit of life abundant for all people. Required Qualifications : Belmont University seeks to attract and retain highly qualified faculty and staff who will support our mission and vision. As a Christ-centered and student-focused community, we aim to: Form diverse leaders of character; Equip people to solve the world’s complex problems through teaching, research and service; And be radical champions for helping people and communities flourish. Knowledge of principles, methods and current developments in the field of study. Knowledge of subject matter and course content taught. Knowledge of instructional strategies and techniques. Demonstrated capacity to engage in high quality scholarly activity. Demonstrated ability to advise, instruct, manage, motivate and evaluate students. Skilled in the use of computers, Internet resources, and MS Office software. Ability to learn relevant sections of BannerWeb, Belmont University’s online integrated database system for student grading. Ability to integrate technology into the teaching and learning process. Ability to successfully interact with students, other educators and educational institution representatives, and the general public in a professional manner. Demonstrated ability to communicate effectively verbally and in writing. Knowledge of the programs and services offered by Belmont University. Interest and ability to work collaboratively in course design and to teach interdisciplinary and topical courses. Ability to work effectively with a wide range of constituencies. Required Education A doctorate degree (DNP, PhD) in nursing is preferred. Consideration will be given to candidates with a terminal degree, or one in progress. Required Experience Preference will be given to candidates with experience in a variety of academic settings and teaching pedagogies. The selected candidate will be required to complete a background check satisfactory to the University. Belmont University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Apply Now Share Save Job Belmont University is a Christ-centered community. The University faculty, administration, and staff uphold Jesus as the Christ and as the measure for all things. As a community seeking to uphold Christian standards of morality, ethics, and conduct, Belmont University holds high expectations of each person who chooses to join the community. In compliance with federal law, including provisions of Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Titles VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, the Age Discrimination in Employment Act and Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973/the Americans with Disabilities Act, Belmont University does not discriminate on the basis of race, sex, color, national or ethnic origin, age, disability, military service, or sexual orientation in its administration of education policies, programs or activities; its admissions policies; or employment. Consistent with applicable civil rights law, the University primarily hires employees of the Christian faith who are committed to support the mission of the University. The University has appointed the Chief Human Resources Officer/Deputy Title IX Coordinator to serve as coordinator of non-discrimination compliance for staff and faculty. The Director of Institutional Equity and Compliance and Title IX Coordinator serves as coordinator of compliance for Title IX (sex discrimination) issues and questions for students. Click here to learn more. *In accordance with accrediting standards for its professional education programs in law and medicine, the University does not apply religious criteria in hiring employees within those programs. All employees hired by the University, regardless of religious faith, shall be committed to Belmont’s Christ-centered, student-focused mission. Belmont's Office of Human Resources will conduct ongoing evaluations of the means by which candidates for employment are sought, to the end that the pool of candidates will include qualified women, minorities, veterans and disabled individuals. Belmont University is an equal opportunity employer under all applicable civil rights laws."
    },
    "https://belmont.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/10/home/requisition/4978?c=belmont": {
      "title": "Director of Recruiting and Admissions",
      "description": "Director of Recruiting and Admissions | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Director of Recruiting and Admissions United States | req4978 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/13/2026 Back to Search Director of Recruiting and Admissions We are now accepting applications for a qualified Director of Recruiting and Admissions at Belmont University. Employment Type Staff Internal Job Category Exempt (Staff) Full-Time Department College of Law Hours 37.5 Primary Duties and Responsibilities: Position purpose: The Director of Recruiting and Admissions provides strategic and operational leadership for the law school’s student recruitment, admissions, and enrollment initiatives. The position is responsible for developing and executing data-informed strategies that attract, engage, and enroll a strong student body; overseeing recruitment programs, personnel, resources, technology, and partnerships; and advising senior leadership on enrollment performance, market conditions, and continuous improvement. Essential Functions: Strategic Enrollment Leadership and Planning Direct the development, implementation, and annual assessment of a comprehensive recruitment strategy aligned with the law school’s enrollment objectives, institutional priorities, and available resources. Implement recruitment goals, enrollment projections, performance measures, and annual operating plans in consultation with the Senior Associate Dean. Exercise independent judgment in prioritizing recruitment markets, prospect segments, communication strategies, travel, and program investments within approved goals and policies. Recruitment, Admissions, and Enrollment Management Lead the full recruitment and applicant-engagement lifecycle from prospect identification through application, admission, deposit, matriculation, and new-student transition. Develop and direct targeted outreach initiatives using the Law School Admission Council’s Candidate Referral Service, admissions technology, and other recruitment resources. Represent the law school at recruitment programs, law school fairs, conferences, and partner events, including extensive travel, and cultivate relationships with pre-law advisors, faculty, alumni, community partners, and referral sources. Program, Event, and Partnership Direction Direct the planning, execution, and evaluation of on-campus and virtual recruitment programs, including information sessions, campus visits, admitted-student programs, and other enrollment initiatives. Oversee program scope, timelines, communications, logistics, resource allocation, and participation by faculty, staff, students, alumni, and external partners. Lead admissions-related components of new-student orientation and coordinate with academic and administrative units to support an effective transition for entering students. Operations, Analytics, Budget, and Compliance Oversee the integrity, effective use, and continuous improvement of admissions databases, prospect records, communication workflows, and recruitment technology. Develop, administer, and monitor the recruitment and admissions operating budget, travel expenditures, program costs, contracts, and vendor relationships within delegated authority. Ensure recruitment activities comply with applicable university policies, accreditation expectations, privacy requirements, and professional standards. Personnel, Program, and Cross-Functional Leadership Provide leadership for recruitment personnel and programs, including assigning work, establishing priorities, training staff, monitoring performance, and supporting professional development, as applicable to the approved organizational structure. Direct the Law Ambassadors program, including recruitment, selection, training, scheduling, standards of conduct, performance expectations, and program assessment. Advise leadership on recruitment strategy, enrollment performance, operational needs, and emerging issues. The above statements describe the job’s essential responsibilities and requirements.  They are not an exhaustive list of the duties that may be assigned to job incumbents. Required Qualifications : Belmont University seeks to attract and retain highly qualified faculty and staff who will support our mission and vision. As a Christ-centered and student-focused community, we aim to: Form diverse leaders of character; Equip people to solve the world’s complex problems through teaching, research and service; And be radical champions for helping people and communities flourish. Three years of experience in recruiting\nis required. Strong organizational,\ninterpersonal, and communication skills are required. The candidate must be proactive and able to\nwork collaboratively. A positive\nattitude, strong work ethic, adaptability, and the ability to multi-task are\nessential. Experience working in a fast-paced environment and the ability to respond to high-pressure situations. Ability to thrive in an environment of hard work. Ability to work effectively with a wide range of constituencies in a diverse community. Required Education Requires a Bachelors Degree Required Experience Requires 3 years of experience in recruiting The selected candidate will be required to complete a background check satisfactory to the University. Belmont University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Apply Now Share Save Job Belmont University is a Christ-centered community. The University faculty, administration, and staff uphold Jesus as the Christ and as the measure for all things. As a community seeking to uphold Christian standards of morality, ethics, and conduct, Belmont University holds high expectations of each person who chooses to join the community. In compliance with federal law, including provisions of Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Titles VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, the Age Discrimination in Employment Act and Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973/the Americans with Disabilities Act, Belmont University does not discriminate on the basis of race, sex, color, national or ethnic origin, age, disability, military service, or sexual orientation in its administration of education policies, programs or activities; its admissions policies; or employment. Consistent with applicable civil rights law, the University primarily hires employees of the Christian faith who are committed to support the mission of the University. The University has appointed the Chief Human Resources Officer/Deputy Title IX Coordinator to serve as coordinator of non-discrimination compliance for staff and faculty. The Director of Institutional Equity and Compliance and Title IX Coordinator serves as coordinator of compliance for Title IX (sex discrimination) issues and questions for students. Click here to learn more. *In accordance with accrediting standards for its professional education programs in law and medicine, the University does not apply religious criteria in hiring employees within those programs. All employees hired by the University, regardless of religious faith, shall be committed to Belmont’s Christ-centered, student-focused mission. Belmont's Office of Human Resources will conduct ongoing evaluations of the means by which candidates for employment are sought, to the end that the pool of candidates will include qualified women, minorities, veterans and disabled individuals. Belmont University is an equal opportunity employer under all applicable civil rights laws."
    },
    "https://belmont.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/10/home/requisition/1484?c=belmont": {
      "title": "Library - Access Services Student Assistant",
      "description": "Library - Access Services Student Assistant | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Library - Access Services Student Assistant United States | req1484 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/13/2026 Back to Search Library - Access Services Student Assistant Employment Type Student Employee Hourly Rate $10.00 Special Note: All students are required to read the BU Student Employment Policy prior to submitting an application. All Federal Work-Study students should read the program rules and regulations located at http://www.belmont.edu/sfs/employment/fws.html Primary Duties and Responsibilities Bunch Library seeks customer service-oriented\nstudent assistants to work in the Access Services Department, answer\ndirectional and basic library-related questions, shelve books and media, and\nmaintain the library collection and physical space. Job Duties: Staff the Information Desk Answer\ndirection and basic library-related questions. Assist patrons with\nlocating/retrieving library materials Refer research questions to the research\nlibrarians Responsible for basic care and upkeep of the library areas. Stacks\nmaintenance including, but not limited to, pulling, shelving, and shifting\nbooks, microform, media and bound periodicals Knowledge of all library\ncollections and the varying circulation policies of each Collect and log\nstatistics Enforce library policies and refer issues to professional library\nstaff as necessary Responsible for working shifts as assigned or arranging for\na substitute Participate in initial and ongoing training on library resources,\npolicies, personnel and procedures Complete tasks assigned by Access Services\nSupervisors, Access Services Manager & Library Director. Required Qualifications Must Be: Friendly and comfortable\ndealing with the general public. Reliable and adhere to the posted\nschedule. Team and task-oriented. Self-motivated and able to\nmultitask. Must be able to push loaded book carts in excess of 100 lbs. Must be able to pick up 50 lbs. Must be able to stand, reach, step up, step down. Additional Information: We accept students regardless of their Federal Work Study status . Applicants who are willing to work 10-15 hours/wk and are\nwilling to cover shifts when available. Scheduled Hours: Applicants must be\nwilling to work at least one late evening until 11pm and on weekends. Monday -\nThursday 7:30am - 12:00am Friday: 7:30am - 7:00pm Saturday: 9:00am - 7:00pm Sunday 1:00pm - 12:00am Required Education Must be enrolled as a student at Belmont University. \nPreference given to students who have completed at least one year of coursework at Belmont. Required Experience Library/Customer service experience preferred. Apply Now Share Save Job Belmont University is a Christ-centered community. The University faculty, administration, and staff uphold Jesus as the Christ and as the measure for all things. As a community seeking to uphold Christian standards of morality, ethics, and conduct, Belmont University holds high expectations of each person who chooses to join the community. In compliance with federal law, including provisions of Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Titles VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, the Age Discrimination in Employment Act and Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973/the Americans with Disabilities Act, Belmont University does not discriminate on the basis of race, sex, color, national or ethnic origin, age, disability, military service, or sexual orientation in its administration of education policies, programs or activities; its admissions policies; or employment. Consistent with applicable civil rights law, the University primarily hires employees of the Christian faith who are committed to support the mission of the University. The University has appointed the Chief Human Resources Officer/Deputy Title IX Coordinator to serve as coordinator of non-discrimination compliance for staff and faculty. The Director of Institutional Equity and Compliance and Title IX Coordinator serves as coordinator of compliance for Title IX (sex discrimination) issues and questions for students. Click here to learn more. *In accordance with accrediting standards for its professional education programs in law and medicine, the University does not apply religious criteria in hiring employees within those programs. All employees hired by the University, regardless of religious faith, shall be committed to Belmont’s Christ-centered, student-focused mission. Belmont's Office of Human Resources will conduct ongoing evaluations of the means by which candidates for employment are sought, to the end that the pool of candidates will include qualified women, minorities, veterans and disabled individuals. Belmont University is an equal opportunity employer under all applicable civil rights laws."
