    "https://belmont.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/10/home/requisition/4971?c=belmont": {
      "title": "Director of Graduate Recruitment & Admissions",
      "description": "Director of Graduate Recruitment & Admissions | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Director of Graduate Recruitment & Admissions United States | req4971 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/1/2026 Back to Search Director of Graduate Recruitment & Admissions We are now accepting applications for a qualified Director of Graduate Recruitment & Admissions at Belmont University. Employment Type Staff Internal Job Category Exempt (Staff) Full-Time Department College of Business Hours 37.5 Primary Duties and Responsibilities: The Director of Graduate Recruitment and Admissions provides leadership for graduate enrollment management for the Jack C. Massey College of Business for all graduate programs of study. These currently include the Professional MBA, Accelerated MBA, Healthcare MBA, Master of Accountancy, and Master of Science in Applied Analytics, as well as several dual-degree programs within and outside of Massey. This position partners with the Associate Dean for Academic Programs and Student Success to develop and execute recruitment, admissions, and yield strategies designed to achieve institutional enrollment objectives, strengthen program competitiveness, and support sustainable growth across graduate business programs. This position guides applicants from inquiry through enrollment, ensures accurate and timely application review, and supports recruitment and retention initiatives through outreach, events, and data tracking. The position works closely with Massey faculty, college leadership, graduate program directors, and campus partners to maintain an efficient, student-centered admissions experience aligned with institutional priorities. Primary position responsibilities: Collaborate with the Dean, Associate Dean, and graduate program directors to achieve enrollment objectives for Massey graduate programs. This includes conducting market research that identifies market opportunities, informs program positioning, and supports decisions regarding program competitiveness and growth. Collaborate with graduate program directors, faculty, and campus partners to align recruitment messaging, admissions criteria, and enrollment processes with academic and institutional priorities. Manage graduate recruitment and outreach initiatives, including communications campaigns, recruitment events, partnership development, and follow-up efforts designed to increase applicant engagement and enrollment yields. Plan and support recruitment and yield events, including graduate information sessions, open houses, fairs, and virtual programming, which may include evening or weekend responsibilities. Direct graduate admissions operations for assigned programs, including application review, verification of materials, and coordination of admissions decisions while maintaining a responsive, student-centered application experience. Cultivate relationships with prospective students throughout the recruitment and admissions cycle, responding to inquiries, guiding applicants through requirements and deadlines, and supporting enrollment decisions. Monitor and analyze enrollment funnel data, including inquiry, application, admission, deposit, and enrollment trends. Generate reports and recommendations to support strategic decision-making and continuous process improvement. Manage budgets related to graduate recruiting activities. Collaborate with Enrollment Services and Student Financial Services on available graduate scholarships and tuition discounts. Collaborate with Enrollment Services and Student Financial Services to make recommendations on graduate scholarships and tuition discounts. Award graduate scholarships and tuition discounts in consultation with the Associate Dean. Supervise Graduate Assistants and student workers, including assigning work, providing training and guidance, monitoring performance, and ensuring timely and high-quality completion of assigned responsibilities. The above statements describe the job’s essential responsibilities and requirements.  They are not an exhaustive list of the duties that may be assigned to job incumbents. Required Qualifications : Belmont University seeks to attract and retain highly qualified faculty and staff who will support our mission and vision. As a Christ-centered and student-focused community, we aim to: Form diverse leaders of character; Equip people to solve the world’s complex problems through teaching, research and service; And be radical champions for helping people and communities flourish. Analytical Thinking: Ability to identify issues, obtain relevant information, relate and compare data from different sources, and identify alternative solutions. Critical Thinking: Interprets and seeks information, uses independent reasoning to diagnose the root cause of situations or issues, identifies and tests solutions and thinks beyond what is typical or customary. Uses information to determine benefits and impact in making decision and/or recommendations. Project/Program/Service Management: Ability to coordinate and administer programs/project activities and protocols. Ability to manage resources, monitor activities, and assess risks and quality issues associated with the program/project. Written and Oral Communications: Ability to present information to individuals or groups; ability to deliver presentations suited to the characteristics and needs of the audience. Ability to convey information clearly and concisely to groups or individuals either verbally or in writing to ensure that they understand the information and the message. Ability to listen and respond appropriately to others. Ability to impact and influence others to further the institution’s strategic objectives. Technical, Computer, and Software Skills: Ability to use Microsoft Office (Excel, PowerPoint, Word) and basic databases and software. Experience using educational CRM platforms like Slate and Business CAS. Experience working in a fast-paced environment and the ability to respond to high-pressure situations. Ability to thrive in an environment of hard work. Ability to work effectively with a wide range of constituencies in a diverse community. Required Education Master's degree required, preferably in Business. Required Experience 1-3 years admissions/recruitment experience in higher education is required, preferably at the graduate level. The selected candidate will be required to complete a background check satisfactory to the University. Belmont University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Apply Now Share Save Job Belmont University is a Christ-centered community. The University faculty, administration, and staff uphold Jesus as the Christ and as the measure for all things. As a community seeking to uphold Christian standards of morality, ethics, and conduct, Belmont University holds high expectations of each person who chooses to join the community. In compliance with federal law, including provisions of Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Titles VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, the Age Discrimination in Employment Act and Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973/the Americans with Disabilities Act, Belmont University does not discriminate on the basis of race, sex, color, national or ethnic origin, age, disability, military service, or sexual orientation in its administration of education policies, programs or activities; its admissions policies; or employment. Consistent with applicable civil rights law, the University primarily hires employees of the Christian faith who are committed to support the mission of the University. The University has appointed the Chief Human Resources Officer/Deputy Title IX Coordinator to serve as coordinator of non-discrimination compliance for staff and faculty. The Director of Institutional Equity and Compliance and Title IX Coordinator serves as coordinator of compliance for Title IX (sex discrimination) issues and questions for students. Click here to learn more. *In accordance with accrediting standards for its professional education programs in law and medicine, the University does not apply religious criteria in hiring employees within those programs. All employees hired by the University, regardless of religious faith, shall be committed to Belmont’s Christ-centered, student-focused mission. Belmont's Office of Human Resources will conduct ongoing evaluations of the means by which candidates for employment are sought, to the end that the pool of candidates will include qualified women, minorities, veterans and disabled individuals. Belmont University is an equal opportunity employer under all applicable civil rights laws."
