    "https://belmont.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/10/home/requisition/4962?c=belmont": {
      "title": "Technology and Innovation Specialist",
      "description": "Technology and Innovation Specialist | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Technology and Innovation Specialist United States | req4962 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/24/2026 Back to Search Technology and Innovation Specialist We are now accepting applications for a qualified Technology and Innovation Specialist at Belmont University. Employment Type Staff Internal Job Category Exempt (Staff) Full-Time Department Service Desk Hours 37.5 Primary Duties and Responsibilities: The Technology and Innovation Specialist at the Thomas F. Frist, Jr. College of Medicine (FCoM) plays a pivotal role in advancing technological integration within the medical education program. This position is central to facilitating seamless collaboration between the medical school's operational units and the University information technology department. The Technology and Innovation Specialist serves as a key liaison, ensuring effective communication and resolution between FCoM and technology vendors. This position is instrumental in driving technological advancements and innovations within the medical education curriculum, contributing significantly to the enhancement of learning experiences and the overall quality of education provided by FCoM. The successful candidate will actively engage in fostering a technologically proficient environment that supports the evolving needs of medical education, aligning with the institution's commitment to excellence in academic programs and student success. Primary position responsibilities: End User Desktop Support: Provide exceptional technical support to end-users within the medical education program, ensuring prompt resolution of hardware and software issues. Assist faculty, staff, and students in troubleshooting, diagnosing, and resolving technology-related problems. Equipment and Software Setup and Integration: Lead the setup, installation, and integration of new equipment and software, focusing on the technical aspects of virtual anatomy and pathology programs. Ensure seamless integration of technology tools into the educational curriculum and operational systems. Collaboration with Operational Units and University Desktop Support: Work collaboratively with operational units within the medical school to assess technology needs and implement effective solutions. Collaborate with the university desktop support team to align and leverage broader technological resources. Vendor Coordination and Problem Resolution: Serve as the liaison between FCoM and technology vendors, coordinating support and troubleshooting for equipment and software specific to the medical education program. Identify, escalate, and resolve technical issues in a timely manner, maintaining strong vendor relationships. Innovation and Continuous Improvement: Proactively explore innovative technologies and solutions to enhance the medical education program's technological infrastructure. Contribute to strategic planning and initiatives aimed at improving technology integration and educational outcomes. Training and Development: Collaboratives with the FCoM Office of Medical Education and Faculty Success to develop and coordinate one-on-one and group training sessions to educate faculty, staff and students. Reviews and creates user guidelines and standard operating procedures for supported hardware infrastructure and academic applications. Other duties as assigned. Required Qualifications : Belmont University seeks to attract and retain highly qualified faculty and staff who will support our mission and vision. As a Christ-centered and student-focused community, we aim to: Form diverse leaders of character; Equip people to solve the world’s complex problems through teaching, research and service; And be radical champions for helping people and communities flourish. Occasional day travel to local hospitals associated with Belmont's medical program is required. Medical information technology background is strongly preferred. An ability to proactively and positively communicate and collaborate with constituents having differing priorities An ability to work as part of a community-minded information technology team while stationed within the constituents' workspace Ability to identify issues, obtain relevant information, relate and compare data from different sources, and identify alternative solutions. Interprets and seeks information, uses independent reasoning to diagnose the root cause of situations or issues, identifies and tests solutions and thinks beyond what is typical or customary. Uses information to determine benefits and impact in making decision and/or recommendations. Ability to use Microsoft Office (Excel, PowerPoint, Word) and basic databases and software. Experience working in a fast-paced environment and the ability to respond to high-pressure situations. Ability to thrive in an environment of hard work. Ability to work effectively with a wide range of constituencies in a diverse community. Required Education An associate's degree is required. A bachelor's degree is preferred. Required Experience 1 - 3 years of related experience required. 4 - 6 years of related experience preferred. A+ technical certification required. The selected candidate will be required to complete a background check satisfactory to the University. Belmont University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Apply Now Share Save Job Belmont University is a Christ-centered community. The University faculty, administration, and staff uphold Jesus as the Christ and as the measure for all things. As a community seeking to uphold Christian standards of morality, ethics, and conduct, Belmont University holds high expectations of each person who chooses to join the community. In compliance with federal law, including provisions of Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Titles VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, the Age Discrimination in Employment Act and Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973/the Americans with Disabilities Act, Belmont University does not discriminate on the basis of race, sex, color, national or ethnic origin, age, disability, military service, or sexual orientation in its administration of education policies, programs or activities; its admissions policies; or employment. Consistent with applicable civil rights law, the University primarily hires employees of the Christian faith who are committed to support the mission of the University. The University has appointed the Chief Human Resources Officer/Deputy Title IX Coordinator to serve as coordinator of non-discrimination compliance for staff and faculty. The Director of Institutional Equity and Compliance and Title IX Coordinator serves as coordinator of compliance for Title IX (sex discrimination) issues and questions for students. Click here to learn more. *In accordance with accrediting standards for its professional education programs in law and medicine, the University does not apply religious criteria in hiring employees within those programs. All employees hired by the University, regardless of religious faith, shall be committed to Belmont’s Christ-centered, student-focused mission. Belmont's Office of Human Resources will conduct ongoing evaluations of the means by which candidates for employment are sought, to the end that the pool of candidates will include qualified women, minorities, veterans and disabled individuals. Belmont University is an equal opportunity employer under all applicable civil rights laws."
    },
    "https://belmont.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/10/home/requisition/4840?c=belmont": {
      "title": "Admissions Coordinator for the College of Sciences and Mathematics",
      "description": "Admissions Coordinator for the College of Sciences and Mathematics | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Admissions Coordinator for the College of Sciences and Mathematics United States | req4840 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/24/2026 Back to Search Admissions Coordinator for the College of Sciences and Mathematics We are now accepting applications for a qualified Admissions Coordinator for the College of Sciences and Mathematics at Belmont University. Employment Type Staff Internal Job Category Exempt (Staff) Full-Time Department Ofc VP for Enrollment Hours 37.5 Primary Duties and Responsibilities: This position involves overseeing admissions counseling,\nrecruitment, and general office tasks for a diverse range of applicants for the College of Sciences and\nMathematics (CSM) and Pre-Health programs. The objective is to manage\nthe enrollment process for various student categories, including transfers,\nre-enrolling students, freshmen, and second-degree candidates. The role\nrequires maintaining a deep understanding of Belmont University's vision and collaborating\nwith admissions counselors, faculty, and various teams to enhance recruitment\nstrategies, coordinate events, and manage the virtual presence of CSM and Pre-Health programs through the website and social media platforms. Additionally, the position\ninvolves reporting on recruitment progress, participating in process\nimprovement teams, and contributing to marketing initiatives for prospective\nstudents. This role will\nhelp with recruitment strategies and admissions presentations for CSM summer\ncamp programs, including specialized engagement initiatives for RISE students.\nFinally, this role will leverage capacity to support broader admissions\nfunctions as needed, including some file review and representation at local\nrecruitment events. Serve as academic and scholarship (if applicable) liaison between Admissions and designated college by maintaining Dean and faculty relations, attending college meetings and events, and representing Admissions at college events. Facilitate daily and virtual college information sessions for prospective families. Partner with admissions visit team for enhanced daily visit and Saturday visit day programming. Work alongside University Marketing to execute the college's marketing plan including the creation of marketing pieces, promotional items, website management, and prospect, alumni and parent outreach, and content for social media channels (including but not limited to CampusESP, Instagram, Facebook, and LinkedIn). Utilize enrollment and university CRMs to analyze data related to the applicant pool and identify trends, demographics, and other patterns to make informed decisions about admissions strategies, targets and departmental scholarships (if applicable). Engage with external constituents to enhance office-wide recruitment efforts. This may include developing relationships and engaging with Belmont alumni, prospective parents, and school or independent college counselors. Other Duties as Assigned Required Qualifications : Belmont University seeks to attract and retain highly qualified faculty and staff who will support our mission and vision. As a Christ-centered and student-focused community, we aim to: Form diverse leaders of character; Equip people to solve the world’s complex problems through teaching, research and service; And be radical champions for helping people and communities flourish. Must possess a current valid driver's license with good driving record. 1 to 3 years of previous private college experience as a student or employee preferred. Experience in the academic subject area of the college is prefered. Experience working in a fast-paced environment and the ability to respond to high-pressure situations. Ability to work effectively with a wide range of constituencies. Required Education Bachelor’s degree required Required Experience Must possess a current valid driver's license with good driving record. 1 to 3 years of previous private college experience as a student or employee preferred. Experience in the academic subject area of the college is preferred. The selected candidate will be required to complete a background check satisfactory to the University. Belmont University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Apply Now Share Save Job Belmont University is a Christ-centered community. The University faculty, administration, and staff uphold Jesus as the Christ and as the measure for all things. As a community seeking to uphold Christian standards of morality, ethics, and conduct, Belmont University holds high expectations of each person who chooses to join the community. In compliance with federal law, including provisions of Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Titles VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, the Age Discrimination in Employment Act and Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973/the Americans with Disabilities Act, Belmont University does not discriminate on the basis of race, sex, color, national or ethnic origin, age, disability, military service, or sexual orientation in its administration of education policies, programs or activities; its admissions policies; or employment. Consistent with applicable civil rights law, the University primarily hires employees of the Christian faith who are committed to support the mission of the University. The University has appointed the Chief Human Resources Officer/Deputy Title IX Coordinator to serve as coordinator of non-discrimination compliance for staff and faculty. The Director of Institutional Equity and Compliance and Title IX Coordinator serves as coordinator of compliance for Title IX (sex discrimination) issues and questions for students. Click here to learn more. *In accordance with accrediting standards for its professional education programs in law and medicine, the University does not apply religious criteria in hiring employees within those programs. All employees hired by the University, regardless of religious faith, shall be committed to Belmont’s Christ-centered, student-focused mission. Belmont's Office of Human Resources will conduct ongoing evaluations of the means by which candidates for employment are sought, to the end that the pool of candidates will include qualified women, minorities, veterans and disabled individuals. Belmont University is an equal opportunity employer under all applicable civil rights laws."
