    "https://belmont.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/10/home/requisition/4140?c=belmont": {
      "title": "Office of Auxiliary Services - Student Worker",
      "description": "Office of Auxiliary Services - Student Worker | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Office of Auxiliary Services - Student Worker United States | req4140 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/16/2026 Back to Search Office of Auxiliary Services - Student Worker Employment Type Student Employee Hourly Rate 15 Special Note: All students are required to read the BU Student Employment Policy prior to submitting an application. All Federal Work-Study students should read the program rules and regulations located at http://www.belmont.edu/sfs/employment/fws.html Primary Duties and Responsibilities This position offers a great opportunity to gain real-world experience while supporting Belmont’s Auxiliary Services. You’ll work in a collaborative team environment and assist with operations for dining, vending, the BruinShop, BruinBooks, and the Mail Center. Scheduling is flexible to accommodate class commitments; however, preference will be given to students who can work a minimum of 8 hours weekly between 8:00 AM and 4:30 PM, Monday through Friday. Primary Duties and Responsibilities Clerical and Office Support Answer phones, respond to emails, and greet visitors in a professional manner Organize files, enter data, and maintain accurate department records Prepare simple reports or documents as needed Vending Operations Visit campus vending machines to ensure they are stocked and functioning properly Report issues promptly and follow up to confirm resolution Track service requests and maintain accurate logs Supporting Campus Dining Operations Monitor video surveillance and report unusual activity in dining and campus convenience stores Respond to technical issues in dining locations and assist with troubleshooting Assist with updates and basic testing for the BruinEats mobile ordering platform Collect student feedback and identify opportunities for service improvement General Department Support Provide assistance with special projects and events within Auxiliary Services Support operations in areas such as Dining, BruinShop, BruinBooks, and the Mail Center as needed Assist with creation of marketing and promotional materials Handle sensitive student information with the utmost professionalism, ensuring all materials are managed and protected in accordance with confidentiality standards Be adaptable and ready to take on new tasks—every day can look a little different! Required Qualifications Strong organizational and analytical skills with attention to detail Excellent communication skills and willingness to work collaboratively with others Self-starter, able to manage and prioritize assignments and deadlines after receiving direction Knowledge of Microsoft Excel, Word, and Teams; general knowledge of Canva preferred Ability to maintain confidentiality and handle sensitive information Required Education Must be enrolled as a student at Belmont University. Required Experience No experience required, but preference will be given to students interested in graphic design and marketing. Apply Now Share Save Job Belmont University is a Christ-centered community. The University faculty, administration, and staff uphold Jesus as the Christ and as the measure for all things. As a community seeking to uphold Christian standards of morality, ethics, and conduct, Belmont University holds high expectations of each person who chooses to join the community. In compliance with federal law, including provisions of Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Titles VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, the Age Discrimination in Employment Act and Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973/the Americans with Disabilities Act, Belmont University does not discriminate on the basis of race, sex, color, national or ethnic origin, age, disability, military service, or sexual orientation in its administration of education policies, programs or activities; its admissions policies; or employment. Consistent with applicable civil rights law, the University primarily hires employees of the Christian faith who are committed to support the mission of the University. The University has appointed the Chief Human Resources Officer/Deputy Title IX Coordinator to serve as coordinator of non-discrimination compliance for staff and faculty. The Director of Institutional Equity and Compliance and Title IX Coordinator serves as coordinator of compliance for Title IX (sex discrimination) issues and questions for students. Click here to learn more. *In accordance with accrediting standards for its professional education programs in law and medicine, the University does not apply religious criteria in hiring employees within those programs. All employees hired by the University, regardless of religious faith, shall be committed to Belmont’s Christ-centered, student-focused mission. Belmont's Office of Human Resources will conduct ongoing evaluations of the means by which candidates for employment are sought, to the end that the pool of candidates will include qualified women, minorities, veterans and disabled individuals. Belmont University is an equal opportunity employer under all applicable civil rights laws."
