      "title": "College of Sciences & Mathematics - Undergraduate Research Laboratory Monitor",
      "description": "College of Sciences & Mathematics - Undergraduate Research Laboratory Monitor | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) College of Sciences & Mathematics - Undergraduate Research Laboratory Monitor United States | req4939 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/11/2026 Back to Search College of Sciences & Mathematics - Undergraduate Research Laboratory Monitor Employment Type Student Employee Hourly Rate 13 Special Note: All students are required to read the BU Student Employment Policy prior to submitting an application. All Federal Work-Study students should read the program rules and regulations located at http://www.belmont.edu/sfs/employment/fws.html Primary Duties and Responsibilities Lab Monitors proctor undergraduate science students conducting research after hours (evenings and weekends). Daily duties and supervision will be provided by the Department of Biology with input from faculty responsible for undergraduate research in labs being monitored. General oversight will be provided by the Department of Biology. Monitor safety of undergraduate science students conducting research. Hourly walk-through of research spaces. Submit nightly reports detailing lab usage and safety adherence. Communicate with Security, research faculty, and Biology Department Chair/Research Coordinator in the event of an emergency. Complete work assignments safely using necessary personal protective equipment and other safety devices. Perform other tasks as assigned. Required Qualifications Applicants must be able to complete and perform essential job functions and responsibilities as specified. Lab Monitors will primarily work in research laboratories without supervision. Adherence to laboratory safety and health policies is required, including the use of all necessary personal protective equipment and other safety devices. Required Education Either currently enrolled as a graduate student at Belmont with a B.A. or B.S. with experience in Biology, Chemis