    "https://belmont.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/10/home/requisition/4930?c=belmont": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Political Science",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Political Science | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Assistant Professor of Political Science United States | req4930 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/1/2026 Back to Search Assistant Professor of Political Science We are now accepting applications for a qualified Assistant Professor of Political Science at Belmont University. Employment Type Faculty Internal Job Category Tenure Track (Faculty) Full-Time Department Political Science Hours N/A Primary Duties and Responsibilities: Primary Duties and Responsibilities: The College of Liberal Arts and Social Sciences at Belmont University\ninvites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position in Political\nScience. The appointment will begin on August 1, 2027. We seek candidates with\nspecializations in comparative politics, especially Asian or Latin American\npolitics, and in political economy, though we will consider candidates with\nother specializations that align with departmental needs and priorities. Job responsibilities include teaching undergraduate political science\nand general education courses. Additional responsibilities include\nacademic advising, student mentoring, scholarly activity, and college and\nuniversity service, and the duties listed below: Complete 24 workload hours, or the equivalent, per academic year. Advise and mentor students in research and other class-related projects. Engage in activities to support the mission and vision of Belmont University and the college in which you teach. Participate in department, college, and university committee work. Engage in scholarly activity and professional development. Advise students in course selection and degree completion. Participate in a local church or faith community and engage with the broader community. Abide by all relevant university, college, and department procedures and policies. Manage the online grading system. Submit book orders in a timely manner. Maintain regular office hours. The above statements describe the job’s essential responsibilities and requirements. They are not an exhaustive list of the duties that may be assigned to job incumbents. Because all Belmont undergraduates complete an innovative\ngeneral education program with significant interdisciplinary components, the\nUniversity particularly seeks applicants who demonstrate an interest in and\nability to collaborate on course design and teach interdisciplinary and topical\ncourses in the program. Application Requirements: During the application process, applicants will be asked\nto submit a cover letter, a curriculum vitae or resume, and a one-page,\n300–400-word essay describing how their core beliefs and practices inform their\nsupport for Belmont’s Christ-centered mission and shape their approaches to\nteaching, research, and service. Review of applications will begin September 21, 2026, and\ncontinue until the position is filled. Belmont University Located near the heart of thriving Nashville, Tennessee,\nBelmont University consists of nearly 9,000 students who come from every state\nand 33 countries. The University is nationally recognized for its innovative\napproach as well as its commitment to undergraduate teaching (U.S. News & World Report). As a Christ-centered, student-focused community, Belmont’s\nmission is to develop diverse leaders of purpose, character and wisdom who\npossess a transformational mindset and are eager and equipped to make the world\na better place. With more than 119 areas of undergraduate study, 60 master’s\nprograms and nine doctoral degrees, Belmont University aims to be the leading\nChrist-centered university in the world, producing leaders who will radically\nchampion the pursuit of life abundant for all people. For more information,\nvisit http://www.belmont.edu. Required Qualifications : Belmont University seeks to attract and retain highly qualified faculty and staff who will support our mission and vision. As a Christ-centered and student-focused community, we aim to: Form diverse leaders of character; Equip people to solve the world’s complex problems through teaching, research and service; And be radical champions for helping people and communities flourish. Knowledge of principles, methods and current developments in the field of study. Knowledge of subject matter and course content taught. Knowledge of instructional strategies and techniques. Demonstrated capacity to engage in high quality scholarly activity. Demonstrated ability to advise, instruct, manage, motivate and evaluate students. Skilled in the use of computers, Internet resources, and MS Office software. Ability to learn relevant sections of BannerWeb, Belmont University’s online integrated database system for student grading. Ability to integrate technology into the teaching and learning process. Ability to successfully interact with students, other educators and educational institution representatives, and the general public in a professional manner. Demonstrated ability to communicate effectively verbally and in writing. Knowledge of the programs and services offered by Belmont University. Interest and ability to work collaboratively in course design and to teach interdisciplinary and topical courses. Ability to work effectively with a wide range of constituencies. Required Education A Ph.D. in political science is required. Candidates who are ABD in the required discipline will be considered. Required Experience Candidates should demonstrate a commitment to effective teaching and the potential to be an outstanding teacher and scholar. The selected candidate will be required to complete a background check satisfactory to the University. Belmont University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Apply Now Share Save Job Belmont University is a Christ-centered community. The University faculty, administration, and staff uphold Jesus as the Christ and as the measure for all things. As a community seeking to uphold Christian standards of morality, ethics, and conduct, Belmont University holds high expectations of each person who chooses to join the community. In compliance with federal law, including provisions of Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Titles VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, the Age Discrimination in Employment Act and Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973/the Americans with Disabilities Act, Belmont University does not discriminate on the basis of race, sex, color, national or ethnic origin, age, disability, military service, or sexual orientation in its administration of education policies, programs or activities; its admissions policies; or employment. Consistent with applicable civil rights law, the University primarily hires employees of the Christian faith who are committed to support the mission of the University. The University has appointed the Chief Human Resources Officer/Deputy Title IX Coordinator to serve as coordinator of non-discrimination compliance for staff and faculty. The Director of Institutional Equity and Compliance and Title IX Coordinator serves as coordinator of compliance for Title IX (sex discrimination) issues and questions for students. Click here to learn more. *In accordance with accrediting standards for its professional education programs in law and medicine, the University does not apply religious criteria in hiring employees within those programs. All employees hired by the University, regardless of religious faith, shall be committed to Belmont’s Christ-centered, student-focused mission. Belmont's Office of Human Resources will conduct ongoing evaluations of the means by which candidates for employment are sought, to the end that the pool of candidates will include qualified women, minorities, veterans and disabled individuals. Belmont University is an equal opportunity employer under all applicable civil rights laws."
    },
    "https://belmont.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/10/home/requisition/4926?c=belmont": {
      "title": "PR/Content Specialist",
      "description": "PR/Content Specialist | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) PR/Content Specialist United States | req4926 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/28/2026 Back to Search PR/Content Specialist We are now accepting applications for a qualified PR/Content Specialist at Belmont University. Employment Type Staff Internal Job Category Exempt (Staff) Full-Time Department Marketing & Communications Hours 37.5 Primary Duties and Responsibilities: The PR/Content Specialist is an early-career storyteller and media relations contributor who uses press releases, media pitches, written stories, website copy and social/video assets to secure earned coverage and deliver compelling content across platforms. This role supports the University's media relations and content marketing efforts by building reporter relationships and producing engaging content for colleges, initiatives and people features, with growing accountability for media placements over time. The ideal candidate is a go-getter with strong communication skills and a passion for media relations and storytelling. Belmont's Office of Communications exists to tell the Belmont story, providing proactive guidance and support to Belmont University in the following areas: Media Relations, Public Relations, Campus and Community Communications, Crisis Communications and Photography. Build and maintain media lists and reporter relationships for assigned areas. Seek content amplification through external and internal outlets, partnering with the content team to discover media opportunities, write press releases and pitch media coverage. Develop social media photo, video and graphic assets to support storytelling and amplify messaging. Craft compelling, high-quality written and multimedia stories highlighting university colleges, initiatives, programs and individuals. Identify and deliver stories that serve recruitment, retention, brand-building and development goals. Ensure all content is delivered on time and in compliance with University brand and style guidelines. Assist with reactive media inquiries and support crisis or sensitive communications situations, coordinating with the PR & Content team and University spokespeople as needed. Conduct keyword research and content gap analysis to inform content strategy in assigned areas. Implement on-page SEO best practices, such as optimizing titles, meta descriptions, headings and internal links for priority website pages. Collaborate with departments and stakeholders to gather information, seeking to become a lead media relations resource for assigned colleges/initiatives. Maintain accurate records in the University's media monitoring platform. Keep up-to-date on media relations and content marketing best practices, seeking continuous improvement and ongoing professional development to advance institutional PR results. Other duties as assigned. Required Qualifications : Belmont University seeks to attract and retain highly qualified faculty and staff who will support our mission and vision. As a Christ-centered and student-focused community, we aim to: Form diverse leaders of character; Equip people to solve the world’s complex problems through teaching, research and service; And be radical champions for helping people and communities flourish. Must have a working knowledge of AP Stylebook. Must have computer proficiency, including Word and Excel. Must know or have ability to learn blog software, blogging best practices and SEO techniques; Belmont Alerts crisis communications system and website content management system. Must be thorough and detail-oriented. Must have excellent oral and written communication skills, including ability to write, edit and proofread. Must have flexibility to work evenings and weekends. An ability to interact constructively with staff and faculty across campus. An ability to work effectively and efficiently to meet deadlines. An ability to possess effective group dynamic skills. Experience working in a fast-paced environment and the ability to respond to high-pressure situations. Ability to thrive in an environment of hard work. An ability to work effectively with a wide range of constituencies in a diverse community. Required Education Bachelor's Degree in Communications, Journalism, English, Public Relations, or related discipline is required.   \nStrong Knowledge of Belmont University preferred. Required Experience At least 3 years in news and public relations with editorial experience preferred. The selected candidate will be required to complete a background check satisfactory to the University. Belmont University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Apply Now Share Save Job Belmont University is a Christ-centered community. The University faculty, administration, and staff uphold Jesus as the Christ and as the measure for all things. As a community seeking to uphold Christian standards of morality, ethics, and conduct, Belmont University holds high expectations of each person who chooses to join the community. In compliance with federal law, including provisions of Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Titles VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, the Age Discrimination in Employment Act and Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973/the Americans with Disabilities Act, Belmont University does not discriminate on the basis of race, sex, color, national or ethnic origin, age, disability, military service, or sexual orientation in its administration of education policies, programs or activities; its admissions policies; or employment. Consistent with applicable civil rights law, the University primarily hires employees of the Christian faith who are committed to support the mission of the University. The University has appointed the Chief Human Resources Officer/Deputy Title IX Coordinator to serve as coordinator of non-discrimination compliance for staff and faculty. The Director of Institutional Equity and Compliance and Title IX Coordinator serves as coordinator of compliance for Title IX (sex discrimination) issues and questions for students. Click here to learn more. *In accordance with accrediting standards for its professional education programs in law and medicine, the University does not apply religious criteria in hiring employees within those programs. All employees hired by the University, regardless of religious faith, shall be committed to Belmont’s Christ-centered, student-focused mission. Belmont's Office of Human Resources will conduct ongoing evaluations of the means by which candidates for employment are sought, to the end that the pool of candidates will include qualified women, minorities, veterans and disabled individuals. Belmont University is an equal opportunity employer under all applicable civil rights laws."
    },
    "https://belmont.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/10/home/requisition/4924?c=belmont": {
      "title": "Web Specialist",
      "description": "Web Specialist | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Web Specialist United States | req4924 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/28/2026 Back to Search Web Specialist We are now accepting applications for a qualified Web Specialist at Belmont University. Employment Type Staff Internal Job Category Exempt (Staff) Full-Time Department Marketing & Communications Hours 37.5 Primary Duties and Responsibilities: The Web Specialist is charged with supporting the production and implementation of content for the web to advance Belmont University’s brand, spread its mission, support its vision and encourage enrollment/investment. The position works collaboratively with University Marketing & Communications colleagues and partners across campus to develop and maintain websites, email communications, online ads and other digital content. Uses analytics and usability testing to make improvements to existing online content and increase online search traffic through search engine optimization. This position works with the members of the Digital Media Team to plan and create engaging, impactful, high-quality digital content through a variety of platforms. In collaboration with University marketing strategy, the Web Specialist will stay abreast of how web content is being consumed and find ways to optimize its findability and share ability across multiple online channels. The Web Specialist will be responsible for delivering web content that is compliant with accessibility and privacy laws. Responsible for supporting the development of web content that effectively and creatively supports the University’s brand and marketing objectives, including, but not limited to, building websites; responsive HTML e-mails; static/animated online ads; interactive media guides; WordPress sites; conversion of static designs to HTML; among others. Build websites from start to finish, including working with partners across campus to evaluate content strategy, develop information architecture, gather content and build websites within the University CMS and other platforms that is in consonance with the University’s brand, content strategy and goals. Ensure that existing content on the University website is up-to-date and meets University marketing objectives through close collaboration with other members of the University marketing and communications team, including but not limited to website copy, photography, video and graphics. Assist in the development and enforcement of University website governance policies through the training of new/existing users and management of the University CMS, Wordpress Multisite and CRM systems. Utilize various measurement and analytics tools to ensure that existing online content is meeting the University’s marketing objectives, as well as evaluating new tools that are not currently in use. Evaluate organic search health on an ongoing basis to improve content to maximize search engine optimization including performing regular SEO audits of important university landing pages. Maintain consecutive ongoing projects, communicating consistently with supervisors and project managers and delivering edits as assigned by assigned deadlines and within budget Draft or suggest web copy to fill content gaps, and review and edit copy submitted by campus partners for university style and brand consistency. Be dedicated to continuous personal and professional development. The above statements describe the job’s essential responsibilities and requirements.  They are not an exhaustive list of the duties that may be assigned to job incumbents. Required Qualifications : Belmont University seeks to attract and retain highly qualified faculty and staff who will support our mission and vision. As a Christ-centered and student-focused community, we aim to: Form diverse leaders of character; Equip people to solve the world’s complex problems through teaching, research and service; And be radical champions for helping people and communities flourish. Experience building websites and email templates using HTML and CSS. Experience using a wide variety of modern web content management systems, customer relationship management systems and other mass email marketing systems Experience with search engine optimization for the web, including experience with Google Search Console. Experience with utilizing analytics tools including, but not limited to, Google Analytics, Google Tag Manager and Google Data Studio to measure success. Experience using Adobe Creative Suite including Photoshop, Illustrator, InDesign and XD. Understanding of storytelling and content strategy for the web. Familiarity with accessibility and privacy laws and how they relate to website design Enthusiasm and ability to produce high quality content on deadline in a fast-paced, high-volume environment with concurrent assignments. Ability to respond to high-pressure situations and to thrive in an environment of hard work. Excellent verbal and written communication skills required, including research, fact-checking, and editing. Exceptional attention to detail, professional demeanor, time management, customer service and the ability to work collaboratively with the highest standards of confidentiality, discretion, and diplomacy. Ability to excel independently and in a team environment. Ability to work effectively with a wide range of constituencies in a diverse community. Familiarity with higher education is a plus. Required Education A Bachelor’s degree in web design, marketing, communications or related field; or an equivalent combination of relevant education and/or experience Required Experience At least two (2) years of relevant professional experience. Portfolio of previous work is required. The selected candidate will be required to complete a background check satisfactory to the University. Belmont University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Apply Now Share Save Job Belmont University is a Christ-centered community. The University faculty, administration, and staff uphold Jesus as the Christ and as the measure for all things. As a community seeking to uphold Christian standards of morality, ethics, and conduct, Belmont University holds high expectations of each person who chooses to join the community. In compliance with federal law, including provisions of Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Titles VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, the Age Discrimination in Employment Act and Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973/the Americans with Disabilities Act, Belmont University does not discriminate on the basis of race, sex, color, national or ethnic origin, age, disability, military service, or sexual orientation in its administration of education policies, programs or activities; its admissions policies; or employment. Consistent with applicable civil rights law, the University primarily hires employees of the Christian faith who are committed to support the mission of the University. The University has appointed the Chief Human Resources Officer/Deputy Title IX Coordinator to serve as coordinator of non-discrimination compliance for staff and faculty. The Director of Institutional Equity and Compliance and Title IX Coordinator serves as coordinator of compliance for Title IX (sex discrimination) issues and questions for students. Click here to learn more. *In accordance with accrediting standards for its professional education programs in law and medicine, the University does not apply religious criteria in hiring employees within those programs. All employees hired by the University, regardless of religious faith, shall be committed to Belmont’s Christ-centered, student-focused mission. Belmont's Office of Human Resources will conduct ongoing evaluations of the means by which candidates for employment are sought, to the end that the pool of candidates will include qualified women, minorities, veterans and disabled individuals. Belmont University is an equal opportunity employer under all applicable civil rights laws."
