    "https://belmont.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/10/home/requisition/4912?c=belmont": {
      "title": "Educational Innovation - Multimedia Production Assistant",
      "description": "Educational Innovation - Multimedia Production Assistant | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Educational Innovation - Multimedia Production Assistant United States | req4912 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/24/2026 Back to Search Educational Innovation - Multimedia Production Assistant Employment Type Student Employee Hourly Rate $13.00 Special Note: All students are required to read the BU Student Employment Policy prior to submitting an application. All Federal Work-Study students should read the program rules and regulations located at http://www.belmont.edu/sfs/employment/fws.html Primary Duties and Responsibilities The Multimedia Production Assistant supports the creation of instructional media assets for a variety of learning experiences. The role spans two complementary areas of work: instructional graphic and interactive media, and video and audio production. Assist the Multimedia Specialist in producing instructional multimedia assets, which may include preparing graphics, iconography, and simple interactive or presentation elements under direction. Assist the Instructional Media Producer in capturing video content, which may include operating cameras, microphones, and lighting equipment during recording sessions. Manage and maintain recording studios, ensuring equipment is set up and functioning properly, and help with setup and teardown for recording sessions. Participate in post-production tasks, including video and audio editing, captioning, and ensuring content quality and accessibility. Help manage and organize multimedia assets within the team's digital asset management system. Collaborate with the instructional design team to understand the project requirements and objectives. Required Qualifications A qualified candidate should bring a strong interest in multimedia production to excel in this role. The ability to learn and adapt to new software and equipment is essential for growth and success. The candidate should also meet these qualifications: Strong organizational skills to maintain an efficient studio environment and keep media assets well-ordered. Effective communication and teamwork skills to collaborate with the instructional design team and other colleagues. Time management and multitasking abilities to meet project deadlines across multiple types of projects. Detail-oriented approach, especially during post-production and accessibility work. Adaptability to a fast-paced and evolving multimedia production environment. Required Education Must be enrolled as a student at Belmont University. Required Experience No experience required. Apply Now Share Save Job Belmont University is a Christ-centered community. The University faculty, administration, and staff uphold Jesus as the Christ and as the measure for all things. As a community seeking to uphold Christian standards of morality, ethics, and conduct, Belmont University holds high expectations of each person who chooses to join the community. In compliance with federal law, including provisions of Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Titles VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, the Age Discrimination in Employment Act and Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973/the Americans with Disabilities Act, Belmont University does not discriminate on the basis of race, sex, color, national or ethnic origin, age, disability, military service, or sexual orientation in its administration of education policies, programs or activities; its admissions policies; or employment. Consistent with applicable civil rights law, the University primarily hires employees of the Christian faith who are committed to support the mission of the University. The University has appointed the Chief Human Resources Officer/Deputy Title IX Coordinator to serve as coordinator of non-discrimination compliance for staff and faculty. The Director of Institutional Equity and Compliance and Title IX Coordinator serves as coordinator of compliance for Title IX (sex discrimination) issues and questions for students. Click here to learn more. *In accordance with accrediting standards for its professional education programs in law and medicine, the University does not apply religious criteria in hiring employees within those programs. All employees hired by the University, regardless of religious faith, shall be committed to Belmont’s Christ-centered, student-focused mission. Belmont's Office of Human Resources will conduct ongoing evaluations of the means by which candidates for employment are sought, to the end that the pool of candidates will include qualified women, minorities, veterans and disabled individuals. Belmont University is an equal opportunity employer under all applicable civil rights laws."
    },
    "https://belmont.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/10/home/requisition/4612?c=belmont": {
      "title": "Belmont Collaborative for Health Systems Innovation & Health Systems Science - Student Office Asst",
      "description": "Belmont Collaborative for Health Systems Innovation & Health Systems Science - Student Office Asst | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Belmont Collaborative for Health Systems Innovation & Health Systems Science - Student Office Asst United States | req4612 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/24/2026 Back to Search Belmont Collaborative for Health Systems Innovation & Health Systems Science - Student Office Asst Employment Type Student Employee Hourly Rate $13 Special Note: All students are required to read the BU Student Employment Policy prior to submitting an application. All Federal Work-Study students should read the program rules and regulations located at http://www.belmont.edu/sfs/employment/fws.html Primary Duties and Responsibilities About the Role The Belmont Collaborative for Health Systems Innovation works at the intersection of healthcare, research, and education — partnering with faculty, fellows, and health system leaders on projects that are actually shaping how care gets delivered. We're looking for a work-study student to join our team as a Student Assistant, supporting the day-to-day work of the department while getting a front-row seat to the research, events, and initiatives that make up the Collaborative's mission. This is a great fit for a student who wants real exposure to health systems work, hands-on experience with communications and project support, and the chance to build relationships with faculty and fellows in the field — not just another admin job. What You'll Do Communications & content: Help manage our social media and LinkedIn presence, update the website, and contribute to marketing materials and newsletters. Research & initiative support: Assist with organizing research initiatives, fundraising efforts, and special projects as they come up. People & events: Serve as a friendly point of contact for faculty, fellows, and students, and help coordinate on-campus events (including some after-hours support when needed). Data & operations: Keep our data organized in Excel and support general office operations — mailings, copies, campus errands, and the like. Special projects: Take on new initiatives as they arise — we welcome students who want to bring ideas to the table. What You'll Gain Direct exposure to health systems innovation work and the people driving it Experience in communications, marketing, and project coordination you can point to on a resume Mentorship and relationship-building with department faculty and fellows A flexible, supportive team environment that works around your academic schedule Hours: 7–10 hours/week, with flexibility around your class schedule. Some remote work possible depending on the project. Location: Primarily in the HSS Department offices at the Thomas F. Frist, Jr. College of Medicine, with occasional remote work for specific projects as approved. Required Qualifications Only applicants with FWS will be considered. Currently enrolled at Belmont University Comfortable handling sensitive information with discretion and confidentially Strong communicator, detail-oriented, and reliable Basic computer skills; familiarity with Microsoft Office (Word, Excel, PowerPoint) is a plus Someone who works well independently and as part of a team Open to new projects and comfortable representing the department professionally No prior experience required — all majors are encouraged to apply Required Education Must be enrolled as a student at Belmont University. Required Experience No experience required. Apply Now Share Save Job Belmont University is a Christ-centered community. The University faculty, administration, and staff uphold Jesus as the Christ and as the measure for all things. As a community seeking to uphold Christian standards of morality, ethics, and conduct, Belmont University holds high expectations of each person who chooses to join the community. In compliance with federal law, including provisions of Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Titles VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, the Age Discrimination in Employment Act and Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973/the Americans with Disabilities Act, Belmont University does not discriminate on the basis of race, sex, color, national or ethnic origin, age, disability, military service, or sexual orientation in its administration of education policies, programs or activities; its admissions policies; or employment. Consistent with applicable civil rights law, the University primarily hires employees of the Christian faith who are committed to support the mission of the University. The University has appointed the Chief Human Resources Officer/Deputy Title IX Coordinator to serve as coordinator of non-discrimination compliance for staff and faculty. The Director of Institutional Equity and Compliance and Title IX Coordinator serves as coordinator of compliance for Title IX (sex discrimination) issues and questions for students. Click here to learn more. *In accordance with accrediting standards for its professional education programs in law and medicine, the University does not apply religious criteria in hiring employees within those programs. All employees hired by the University, regardless of religious faith, shall be committed to Belmont’s Christ-centered, student-focused mission. Belmont's Office of Human Resources will conduct ongoing evaluations of the means by which candidates for employment are sought, to the end that the pool of candidates will include qualified women, minorities, veterans and disabled individuals. Belmont University is an equal opportunity employer under all applicable civil rights laws."
    },
    "https://belmont.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/10/home/requisition/4125?c=belmont": {
      "title": "College of Liberal Arts & Social Sciences - Student Worker",
      "description": "College of Liberal Arts & Social Sciences - Student Worker | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) College of Liberal Arts & Social Sciences - Student Worker United States | req4125 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/24/2026 Back to Search College of Liberal Arts & Social Sciences - Student Worker Employment Type Student Employee Hourly Rate $13.00 Special Note: All students are required to read the BU Student Employment Policy prior to submitting an application. All Federal Work-Study students should read the program rules and regulations located at http://www.belmont.edu/sfs/employment/fws.html Primary Duties and Responsibilities Support Program Assistant for the School of Humanities and School of Theology & Christian Ministry to assist in various administrative tasks including, but not limited to: Filing and organizing, printing, copying, scanning, etc. Greet and assist faculty, staff, students, and guests with general questions about CLASS and Belmont University broadly. Maintain the cleanliness of the office reception area, workrooms, and storage rooms. Assist with organization, inventory, and stocking of office supplies for faculty and staff. Sort mail into appropriate faculty mailboxes and assist in mail delivery. Be prepared to assist with various tasks related to the support of CLASS faculty, staff, and students. Position is mostly sitting at a front desk or in the workroom. May require lifting items up to 30 lbs. Required Qualifications MUST qualify for Federal Work Study to be considered Must possess a professional & positive demeanor, while having good social etiquette Must be punctual, detail-oriented, and able to maintain confidentiality Must be self-motivated and exhibit excellent communicaition skills Must have a willingness to learn new skills Required Education Must be enrolled as a student at Belmont University. Required Experience No experience required. Apply Now Share Save Job Belmont University is a Christ-ce