    "https://belmont.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/10/home/requisition/1482?c=belmont": {
      "title": "O'More College of Architecture, Art & Design - Building Monitor",
      "description": "O'More College of Architecture, Art & Design - Building Monitor | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) O'More College of Architecture, Art & Design - Building Monitor United States | req1482 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/24/2026 Back to Search O'More College of Architecture, Art & Design - Building Monitor Employment Type Student Employee Hourly Rate $13.00 Special Note: All students are required to read the BU Student Employment Policy prior to submitting an application. All Federal Work-Study students should read the program rules and regulations located at http://www.belmont.edu/sfs/employment/fws.html Primary Duties and Responsibilities The Building Monitor’s\npurpose is to monitor the people coming in and out of the CAD facility, to maintain a safe and secure environment, and to communicate\nany issues related to the safety and security of the building to the appropriate\nstaff person(s). The Building Monitor will arrive for his/her shift promptly as\nscheduled and maintain responsibility for the safety and security of the facility. The Building Monitor will\nconduct hourly rounds of the facility so that he/she is aware of who is\nin the building and to look for any maintenance or security needs. The\nBuilding Monitor will greet students, faculty/staff, or guests who are using\nthe facility after hours and on weekends. The Building Monitor will\ncommunicate any issues or concerns related to the safety and security of the facility or any incidents that occur while on duty with the appropriate\nstaff person and/or Campus Security. Occasionally requires standing, lifting,\npulling, pushing, and carrying, reaching both high and low. Frequently requires\nwalking and balancing. Constantly requires sitting, repetitious finder and\nwrist movement, speaking clearly, hearing conversations, hearing (with acuity),\nseeing near and far with depth perception and color vision. Required Qualifications The ideal candidate will be reliable and punctual, able to work\nindependently with little supervision, able to work well with peers, and an\nexcellent communicator. Required Education Must be currently enrolled as a student in O'More College of Architecture & Design Required Experience Previous work experience preferred, but not required. Apply Now Share Save Job Belmont University is a Christ-centered community. The University faculty, administration, and staff uphold Jesus as the Christ and as the measure for all things. As a community seeking to uphold Christian standards of morality, ethics, and conduct, Belmont University holds high expectations of each person who chooses to join the community. In compliance with federal law, including provisions of Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Titles VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, the Age Discrimination in Employment Act and Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973/the Americans with Disabilities Act, Belmont University does not discriminate on the basis of race, sex, color, national or ethnic origin, age, disability, military service, or sexual orientation in its administration of education policies, programs or activities; its admissions policies; or employment. Consistent with applicable civil rights law, the University primarily hires employees of the Christian faith who are committed to support the mission of the University. The University has appointed the Chief Human Resources Officer/Deputy Title IX Coordinator to serve as coordinator of non-discrimination compliance for staff and faculty. The Director of Institutional Equity and Compliance and Title IX Coordinator serves as coordinator of compliance for Title IX (sex discrimination) issues and questions for students. Click here to learn more. *In accordance with accrediting standards for its professional education programs in law and medicine, the University does not apply religious criteria in hiring employees within those programs. All employees hired by the University, regardless of religious faith, shall be committed to Belmont’s Christ-centered, student-focused mission. Belmont's Office of Human Resources will conduct ongoing evaluations of the means by which candidates for employment are sought, to the end that the pool of candidates will include qualified women, minorities, veterans and disabled individuals. Belmont University is an equal opportunity employer under all applicable civil rights laws."
