    "https://belmont.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/10/home/requisition/4902?c=belmont": {
      "title": "Food Pantry - Nourishing Network Program Assistant",
      "description": "Food Pantry - Nourishing Network Program Assistant | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Food Pantry - Nourishing Network Program Assistant United States | req4902 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/14/2026 Back to Search Food Pantry - Nourishing Network Program Assistant Employment Type Student Employee Hourly Rate $15.00 Special Note: All students are required to read the BU Student Employment Policy prior to submitting an application. All Federal Work-Study students should read the program rules and regulations located at http://www.belmont.edu/sfs/employment/fws.html Primary Duties and Responsibilities Primary Duties\n& Responsibilities: - Oversee the daily operations of the campus pantry, ensuring efficient distribution of food, hygiene products, and essential supplies. - Manage inventory systems of the campus pantry by monitoring stock levels, forecasting needs, and maintaining accurate inventory records and reports. - Monitor pantry utilization by maintaining accurate records and analyzing trends to support program planning. - Coordinate the receipt, inspection, sorting, and organization of donated items to ensure quality and efficient storage. - Establish and maintain standards for the cleanliness, organization, safety, and functionality of pantry storage and distribution spaces. - Assist in the management and administration of the Swipe Out Hunger program by coordinating meal swipe donations, supporting program operations, and maintaining records. - Lead marketing and outreach initiatives for the Nourishing Network, including the Swipe Out Hunger program, pantry events, food and meal swipe donation drives, and volunteer recruitment. - Provide leadership to volunteers and student employees by fostering a service-oriented environment and ensuring adherence to policies and procedures. - Collaborate with campus departments and community partners to expand resources, strengthen partnerships, and enhance the overall impact of 