    "https://belmont.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/10/home/requisition/2056?c=belmont": {
      "title": "Begin Anew - Children's Program Assistant",
      "description": "Begin Anew - Children's Program Assistant | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Begin Anew - Children's Program Assistant United States | req2056 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/14/2026 Back to Search Begin Anew - Children's Program Assistant Employment Type Student Employee Hourly Rate $18.00 Special Note: All students are required to read the BU Student Employment Policy prior to submitting an application. All Federal Work-Study students should read the program rules and regulations located at http://www.belmont.edu/sfs/employment/fws.html Primary Duties and Responsibilities Under guidance and direction of the Children’s Program Coordinator, the Children’s Program Assistant will assist in executing the 3 components of our Children’s Programming: Bible Study, homework help, and craft or playtime, at a specific campus. This person will consistently offer a high level of excellence and care in Children’s Programming for children aged infant‐5th grade. • Assist in conducting age‐appropriate activities for the children ﴾infant through 5th grade﴿. This will include a Bible study, help with homework as needed, and time for play • Aid elementary‐aged children with homework and provide tutoring in math, literacy, reading, and other subjects. • Perform other duties as assigned There are two location that are available: Woodbine and Madison. Works in well-lit, ventilated and climate-controlled environment. Noise level in the work environment is typical for a childcare or school environment. The physical demands are representative of those that must be met to successfully perform the essential duties of this job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential job duties. While performing the duties of this job, the colleague is occasionally required to stand; walk; sit for extended periods of time; use hands to handle or feel objects, tools or controls; reach with hands and arms; climb stairs; balance; stoop, kneel, bend, crouch, or crawl; speak or hear. The colleague must occasionally lift, push, pull and/or move up to 20 pounds. Required Qualifications This is an off‐campus position. Applicants MUST have Federal Work Study and reliable means of transportation to be considered . Training and resources will be provided to you by the Program Manager and/or Children’s Program Coordinator. Required Education Must be enrolled as a student at Belmont University. Required Experience ●\tExperience working with children, preferably in a church or Christian environment\n●\tWillingness to work with different cultures and faith beliefs\n●\tPleasant and calm demeanor in working with children, staff members, volunteers, and others Apply Now Share Save Job Belmont University is a Christ-centered community. The University faculty, administration, and staff uphold Jesus as the Christ and as the measure for all things. As a community seeking to uphold Christian standards of morality, ethics, and conduct, Belmont University holds high expectations of each person who chooses to join the community. In compliance with federal law, including provisions of Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Titles VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, the Age Discrimination in Employment Act and Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973/the Americans with Disabilities Act, Belmont University does not discriminate on the basis of race, sex, color, national or ethnic origin, age, disability, military service, or sexual orientation in its administration of education policies, programs or activities; its admissions policies; or employment. Consistent with applicable civil rights law, the University primarily hires employees of the Christian faith who are committed to support the mission of the University. The University has appointed the Chief Human Resources Officer/Deputy Title IX Coordinator to serve as coordinator of non-discrimination compliance for staff and 