    "https://belmont.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/10/home/requisition/1647?c=belmont": {
      "title": "Begin Anew - Adult High School Equivalency Tutor",
      "description": "Begin Anew - Adult High School Equivalency Tutor | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Begin Anew - Adult High School Equivalency Tutor United States | req1647 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/14/2026 Back to Search Begin Anew - Adult High School Equivalency Tutor Employment Type Student Employee Hourly Rate $18.00 Special Note: All students are required to read the BU Student Employment Policy prior to submitting an application. All Federal Work-Study students should read the program rules and regulations located at http://www.belmont.edu/sfs/employment/fws.html Primary Duties and Responsibilities Adult Education High School Equivalency (HSE) Tutor will agree to uphold\nthe mission, vision, and statement of faith of Begin Anew. Under the guidance\nand direction of the Program Manager, the HSE Tutor will: Assist adult\nstudents in a classroom setting with preparation for the High School\nEquivalency (GED) test in one of five subjects: Math, Reading, Writing, Social\nStudies, Science. Instruction is one-on-one or in a small group. Tutors can\nrequest a subject they are most comfortable instructing in, and teaching\nmaterials with answer keys are provided by the Program Manager. Update each\nstudent’s weekly work log indicating subject areas studied and next steps. Develop relationships with students. Assist Childcare Coordinator with Story\nTime and Play Time. May include infant care including feeding, diapering, etc. May include assisting the Program Manager in class set up for the evening. Positions are open in: *Franklin on Tuesday and Thursday evenings *Madison on Monday and Thursday evenings *Crievewood on Tuesday and Thursday evenings *Woodbine area on Monday and Thursday evenings Required Qualifications Applicants MUST have Federal Work-Study in order to be considered. MUST have reliable means of transportation. Applicant\nmust have computer and access to the internet. Ability to explain Math and/or English to adult stude