    "https://belmont.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/10/home/requisition/4119?c=belmont": {
      "title": "Office of Alumni Engagement - Student Assistant",
      "description": "Office of Alumni Engagement - Student Assistant | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Office of Alumni Engagement - Student Assistant United States | req4119 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/12/2026 Back to Search Office of Alumni Engagement - Student Assistant Employment Type Student Employee Hourly Rate $13.00 Special Note: All students are required to read the BU Student Employment Policy prior to submitting an application. All Federal Work-Study students should read the program rules and regulations located at http://www.belmont.edu/sfs/employment/fws.html Primary Duties and Responsibilities Job Summary: The Office of Alumni Engagement is seeking a motivated and organized part-time student worker to assist with various tasks and events. This position is ideal for students who are enthusiastic about event planning, detail-oriented, and looking to gain experience in a professional office setting. The student worker will support the alumni office team in organizing and executing events, ranging from almost-alumni events for graduating seniors to alumni reunions and other special occasions.  This role will also support daily operations of the Alumni Engagement team. Key Responsibilities: Event Preparation and Support: Assist in the planning and execution of alumni events, including almost-alumni events, reunions, and other special programs. Prepare materials for events such as nametags, guest lists, and event signage. Provide on-site support during events, including greeting guests, assisting with registration, and ensuring smooth event operations. Assist in preparing and packing needed materials prior to an event and reorganizing post event Administrative Tasks: Assist with data entry and updating alumni contact information in the database. Prepare and assemble event materials, such as programs, brochures, and thank-you gifts. Manage and organize event supplies and inventory. Assisting in hosting alumni and guests in the Foutch Alumni House. Perform general office duties, including answering phones, responding to emails, and filing documents. Communication and Outreach: Collaborate with the alumni office team to develop and implement creative ideas for engaging alumni and current students. This position will report to the Foutch Alumni House with occasional opportunities for remote work. Ability to lift up to 50 pounds and climb stairs. The Foutch Alumni House does not have elevator access to the second floor. Required Qualifications Strong organizational skills and attention to detail. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills. Ability to work independently and as part of a team. Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite (Word, Excel, PowerPoint) and comfortable using email and social media platforms. Required Education Must be enrolled as a student at Belmont University. Required Experience Previous event-related or office experience preferred but not required. Apply Now Share Save Job Belmont University is a Christ-centered community. The University faculty, administration, and staff uphold Jesus as the Christ and as the measure for all things. As a community seeking to uphold Christian standards of morality, ethics, and conduct, Belmont University holds high expectations of each person who chooses to join the community. In compliance with federal law, including provisions of Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Titles VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, the Age Discrimination in Employment Act and Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973/the Americans with Disabilities Act, Belmont University does not discriminate on the basis of race, sex, color, national or ethnic origin, age, disability, military service, or sexual orientation in its administration of education policies, programs or activities; its admissions policies; or employment. Consistent with applicable civil rights law, the University primarily hires employees of the Christian faith who are committed to support the mission of the University. The University has appointed the Chief Human Resources Officer/Deputy Title IX Coordinator to serve as coordinator of non-discrimination compliance for staff and faculty. The Director of Institutional Equity and Compliance and Title IX Coordinator serves as coordinator of compliance for Title IX (sex discrimination) issues and questions for students. Click here to learn more. *In accordance with accrediting standards for its professional education programs in law and medicine, the University does not apply religious criteria in hiring employees within those programs. All employees hired by the University, regardless of religious faith, shall be committed to Belmont’s Christ-centered, student-focused mission. Belmont's Office of Human Resources will conduct ongoing evaluations of the means by which candidates for employment are sought, to the end that the pool of candidates will include qualified women, minorities, veterans and disabled individuals. Belmont University is an equal opportunity employer under all applicable civil rights laws."
    },
    "https://belmont.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/10/home/requisition/2723?c=belmont": {
      "title": "College of Liberal Arts & Social Sciences - Admissions and Social Media Assistant",
      "description": "College of Liberal Arts & Social Sciences - Admissions and Social Media Assistant | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) College of Liberal Arts & Social Sciences - Admissions and Social Media Assistant United States | req2723 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/12/2026 Back to Search College of Liberal Arts & Social Sciences - Admissions and Social Media Assistant Employment Type Student Employee Hourly Rate $13 Special Note: All students are required to read the BU Student Employment Policy prior to submitting an application. All Federal Work-Study students should read the program rules and regulations located at http://www.belmont.edu/sfs/employment/fws.html Primary Duties and Responsibilities Are you a creative person who loves sharing\nabout the Belmont experience? If you are looking for ways to grow your\nleadership skills & help others, the Admissions Assistant position may be a\ngreat fit for you! The Admissions and Social Media Assistant for the College of Liberal Arts\n& Social Sciences will serve as a representative of the college while\ncollaborating with the Admissions Coordinator to complete administrative tasks,\noccasionally join and lead academic information session presentations for\nprospective students, create content and post on social media. Collaborate with the Admissions Coordinator to create social media content that highlights student experiences, academic programs, and campus events. Attend admissions and campus events to capture photos and videos for social media. Assist with editing content for Instagram, TikTok, and other platforms (experience preferred but not required). Brainstorm and contribute creative ideas for recruitment and engagement campaigns. Support admissions events and help welcome prospective students and families. (Preview Days and Be Belmont Day) Assist with administrative tasks such as organizing materials, filing, data entry, and other office projects as needed. Learn about the admissions process, recruitment strategies, and the academic programs within CLASS. Learn and occasionally lead college academic information sessions if class schedule allows Support Coordinator in various administrative tasks such as writing and mailing postcards to prospective students, printing and mailing letters, assembling admit gift packages, etc. Assist in preparation for large visit days including Preview Days, Future Bruin Fridays & Be Belmont Day Required Qualifications Must possess a professional & positive\ndemeanor, while having good phone and social etiquette Strong communication and organizational skills. Must be punctual, detail-oriented, and able to\nmaintain confidentiality Must have a willingness to learn new\nskills Must be proficient in Word, Excel & social\nchannels including Instagram, Facebook & LinkedIn Must have Federal Work Study to be\nconsidered Must be available to work at least two to\nthree days out of the week for a minimum of 2 hours each day Preferred skills: Competent interpersonal communication and\npublic speaking abilities Knowledgeable in Canva & willing to learn\nand follow best practices when posting to Instagram, Facebook & LinkedIn Willingness to stay up to date on social media\ntrends that will increase engagement and are appropriate for the college to\nparticipate in Experience with professional photography\npreferred Great penmanship preferred Photography, videography, or editing experience is a plus, but not required. Student will\npreferably be engaged socially within the College of Liberal Arts and Social\nSciences in order to stay informed about current student events and create\ncontent Required Education Must be enrolled as a student at Belmont University. Would be a great job for Social Media Management, Marketing, Communications, Corporate Communications, Journalism, and Public Relations majors. Required Experience Prior experience preferred but not required. Apply Now Share Save Job Belmont University is a Christ-centered community. The University faculty, administration, and staff uphold Jesus as the Christ and as the measure for all things. As a community seeking to uphold Christian standards of morality, ethics, and conduct, Belmont University holds high expectations of each person who chooses to join the community. In compliance with federal law, including provisions of Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Titles VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, the Age Discrimination in Employment Act and Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973/the Americans with Disabilities Act, Belmont University does not discriminate on the basis of race, sex, color, national or ethnic origin, age, disability, military service, or sexual orientation in its administration of education policies, programs or activities; its admissions policies; or employment. Consistent with applicable civil rights law, the University primarily hires employees of the Christian faith who are committed to support the mission of the University. The University has appointed the Chief Human Resources Officer/Deputy Title IX Coordinator to serve as coordinator of non-discrimination compliance for staff and faculty. The Director of Institutional Equity and Compliance and Title IX Coordinator serves as coordinator of compliance for Title IX (sex discrimination) issues and questions for students. Click here to learn more. *In accordance with accrediting standards for its professional education programs in law and medicine, the University does not apply religious criteria in hiring employees within those programs. All employees hired by the University, regardless of religious faith, shall be committed to Belmont’s Christ-centered, student-focused mission. Belmont's Office of Human Resources will conduct ongoing evaluations of the means by which candidates for employment are sought, to the end that the pool of candidates will include qualified women, minorities, veterans and disabled individuals. Belmont University is an equal opportunity employer under all applicable civil rights laws."
