    "https://belmont.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/10/home/requisition/4118?c=belmont": {
      "title": "Office of Alumni Engagement - Student Communications & Social Media Assistant",
      "description": "Office of Alumni Engagement - Student Communications & Social Media Assistant | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Office of Alumni Engagement - Student Communications & Social Media Assistant United States | req4118 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/11/2026 Back to Search Office of Alumni Engagement - Student Communications & Social Media Assistant Employment Type Student Employee Hourly Rate $13.00 Special Note: All students are required to read the BU Student Employment Policy prior to submitting an application. All Federal Work-Study students should read the program rules and regulations located at http://www.belmont.edu/sfs/employment/fws.html Primary Duties and Responsibilities Job Description: Are you passionate about creating compelling social\nmedia content and eager to gain experience in a collaborative team environment?\nBelmont’s Office of Alumni Engagement is seeking a creative and motivated Communications & Social Media Assistant to join our team. This position offers an exciting\nopportunity to engage with our alumni community and support the enhancement of\nour social media presence. Key Responsibilities: Content Creation & Social Media Management : •     Designing assets for social media content including graphics, reels and captions •     Scheduling & publishing content on Instagram, Facebook & LinkedIn •     Tracking analytics and drawing conclusions from them for how to improve content performance •     Researching current social media trends, especially in peer alumni programs at other universities •     Contributing creative ideas for how to increase and sustain social media engagement •     Monitor and respond to comments, messages and inquiries on social media platforms promptly and professionally •     Engage with alumni by highlighting their achievements and contributions through posts and stories Administrative Support: Organize and manage the email inbox for alumni@belmont.edu, ensuring that emails reach the relevant team member. Provide general administrative support to the Alumni Office as needed, including answering the office phone, covering the front desk and assisting with key alumni events. The position will mostly be in the Foutch Alumni House, with occasional opportunities for remote work. Required Qualifications Proficiency in social media platforms (Instagram, Facebook & LinkedIn) and basic knowledge of social media management tools. Strong writing, editing and communication skills. Ability to work independently and manage multiple tasks effectively. Creative and detail-oriented with a passion for storytelling and digital content creation. Prior experience with graphic design tools (e.g. Canva, Adobe Creative Suite) is a plus but not required. If you have experience in graphic design and/or content creation, you will be asked to include pieces of your portfolio as a part of the interview process. Required Education Must be enrolled as a student at Belmont University. Ideal candidates have a major or strong interest in Communications, Marketing, Digital Media, or a related field. Required Experience Prior communication and/or social media experience is preferred but not required. Apply Now Share Save Job Belmont University is a Christ-centered community. The University faculty, administration, and staff uphold Jesus as the Christ and as the measure for all things. As a community seeking to uphold Christian standards of morality, ethics, and conduct, Belmont University holds high expectations of each person who chooses to join the community. In compliance with federal law, including provisions of Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Titles VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, the Age Discrimination in Employment Act and Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973/the Americans with Disabilities Act, Belmont University does not discriminate on the basis of race, sex, color, national or ethnic origin, age, disability, military service, or sexual orientation in its administration of education policies, programs or activities; its admissions policies; or employment. Consistent with applicable civil rights law, the University primarily hires employees of the Christian faith who are committed to support the mission of the University. The University has appointed the Chief Human Resources Officer/Deputy Title IX Coordinator to serve as coordinator of non-discrimination compliance for staff and faculty. The Director of Institutional Equity and Compliance and Title IX Coordinator serves as coordinator of compliance for Title IX (sex discrimination) issues and questions for students. Click here to learn more. *In accordance with accrediting standards for its professional education programs in law and medicine, the University does not apply religious criteria in hiring employees within those programs. All employees hired by the University, regardless of religious faith, shall be committed to Belmont’s Christ-centered, student-focused mission. Belmont's Office of Human Resources will conduct ongoing evaluations of the means by which candidates for employment are sought, to the end that the pool of candidates will include qualified women, minorities, veterans and disabled individuals. Belmont University is an equal opportunity employer under all applicable civil rights laws."
    },
    "https://belmont.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/10/home/requisition/1408?c=belmont": {
      "title": "CEMB - REM Front Desk Worker",
      "description": "CEMB - REM Front Desk Worker | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) CEMB - REM Front Desk Worker United States | req1408 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/11/2026 Back to Search CEMB - REM Front Desk Worker Employment Type Student Employee Hourly Rate $13.00 Special Note: All students are required to read the BU Student Employment Policy prior to submitting an application. All Federal Work-Study students should read the program rules and regulations located at http://www.belmont.edu/sfs/employment/fws.html Primary Duties and Responsibilities This person in the\nposition would serve as the \"front desk\" for the production rooms in\nthe REM Studio's on weekdays (2pm-2am) and weekends (8am-2am). Times will\nvary. The student worker will keep a log students and\nvisitors to REM Studio. Perform other duties as requested. Monitor use of\nclassrooms for assigned labs. Assist Staff Engineers and Studio Manager as\nneeded. Required Qualifications Applicant must have Federal Work-Study (FWS) Award for current year. Experience with MSOffice required. Experience with Mac OS required. MUST be punctual and reliable. Required Education Must be a Belmont University student. AET and MBU are preferred but not required. Required Experience No experience needed. Apply Now Share Save Job Belmont University is a Christ-centered community. The University faculty, administration, and staff uphold Jesus as the Christ and as the measure for all things. As a community seeking to uphold Christian standards of morality, ethics, and conduct, Belmont University holds high expectations of each person who chooses to join the community. In compliance with federal law, including provisions of Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Titles VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, the Age Discrimination in Employment Act and Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973/the Americans with Disabilities Act, Belmont University does not discriminate on the ba