      "description": "School of Music - Production Crew | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) School of Music - Production Crew United States | req1391 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/11/2026 Back to Search School of Music - Production Crew Employment Type Student Employee Hourly Rate $13.00 Special Note: All students are required to read the BU Student Employment Policy prior to submitting an application. All Federal Work-Study students should read the program rules and regulations located at http://www.belmont.edu/sfs/employment/fws.html Primary Duties and Responsibilities Assist in audio and general set up for event operations Moving and lifting equipment such as chairs, stands, production equipment, etc. Hours are not regular. All students interested in positions please include general info regarding experience and education. Required Qualifications None - for stage set-up crew any applicant can be trained. Some - for skilled crew. Qualified Music Student applicants will be used in the following sub-positions: Front of House/Monitor Mixing, Stage Manager, Wireless Mic Techs, etc. Must be able to move and lift equipment up to 50lbs Required Education Must be enrolled as a current student at Belmont University. Required Experience None – for stage set-up crew any applicant can be trained.\nSome – for skilled crew. Qualified Music Student applicants will be used in the following sub-positions: Front of House/Monitor Mixing, Stage Manager, Wireless Mic Techs, etc. Apply Now Share Save Job Belmont University is a Christ-centered community. The University faculty, administration, and staff uphold Jesus as the Christ and as the measure for all things. As a community seeking to uphold Christian standards of morality, ethics, and conduct, Belmont University holds high expectations of each person who chooses to join the community. In compliance with federal law, including provisions of Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Titles VI and VII of th