    "https://belmont.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/10/home/requisition/2441?c=belmont": {
      "title": "Rejoice School of Ballet - Teaching Assistant",
      "description": "Rejoice School of Ballet - Teaching Assistant | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Rejoice School of Ballet - Teaching Assistant United States | req2441 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/10/2026 Back to Search Rejoice School of Ballet - Teaching Assistant Employment Type Student Employee Hourly Rate $15.00 Special Note: All students are required to read the BU Student Employment Policy prior to submitting an application. All Federal Work-Study students should read the program rules and regulations located at http://www.belmont.edu/sfs/employment/fws.html Primary Duties and Responsibilities This is an off-campus position only and applicant must have FWS to be considered. Rejoice School of Ballet is a non-profit dance studio that provides high quality dance training to children from diverse racial, cultural, and socioeconomic backgrounds. Rejoice seeks to provide a loving and safe environment for kids to foster their creativity, and to participate in an activity (dance) that will teach them qualities and skills to be successful later in life, regardless of their individual goals and pursuits. Rejoice Teaching Assistants help out in our children's ballet classes and serve as an assistant to the primary instructor. While the Instructor runs class, the Teaching Assistant is in the studio: Assist the lead teacher with children's dance classes,\nhelping demonstrate proper class participation, and gently redirecting\nstudents' attention as needed. Shifts are available during after-school hours (3:00-7:30 PM) on weekdays, and Saturday mornings. We are looking for Teaching Assistants to assist at all four Rejoice locations: East Nashville, Hadley Park Community Center, Barefoot Republic Community Center, and Smith Springs Community Center. All four locations are 20-30 minutes from Belmont's campus. Ability to participate in children's dance class, getting up\nand down off the floor, and being on feet for 45-60 minutes at a time. Some\nlight lifting will be required (boxes, chairs, dance costumes, etc). Required Qualifications Rejoice School of Ballet expects Teaching Assistants to have the following qualifications: (1) Must have Federal Work Study and reliable transportation to get to and from locations that are 20-30 mins away from Belmont. (2) A background in dance (enough to participate in children's classes). The ideal candidate would have a strong enough dance background to serve as a backup to the primary Instructor, being able to step in and take over for the instructor if they are sick or late, though this is not a requirement. (3)Experience working with children in a large group setting, including children from racially and socioeconomically diverse communities. (4) Consistently punctual, reliable, and responsible. Able to act as a role model to the students at Rejoice School of Ballet. Required Education Must be enrolled as a student at Belmont University. Students studying Dance, Education, or Early Childhood Development are preferred but not required. Required Experience Some dance experience is required; experience working with kids is strongly preferred but not required. Apply Now Share Save Job Belmont University is a Christ-centered community. The University faculty, administration, and staff uphold Jesus as the Christ and as the measure for all things. As a community seeking to uphold Christian standards of morality, ethics, and conduct, Belmont University holds high expectations of each person who chooses to join the community. In compliance with federal law, including provisions of Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Titles VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, the Age Discrimination in Employment Act and Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973/the Americans with Disabilities Act, Belmont University does not discriminate on the basis of race, sex, color, national or ethnic origin, age, disability, military service, or sexual orientation in its administration of education policies, programs or activities; its admissions policies; or employment. Consistent with applicable civil rights law, the University primarily hires employees of the Christian faith who are committed to support the mission of the University. The University has appointed the Chief Human Resources Officer/Deputy Title IX Coordinator to serve as coordinator of non-discrimination compliance for staff and faculty. The Director of Institutional Equity and Compliance and Title IX Coordinator serves as coordinator of compliance for Title IX (sex discrimination) issues and questions for students. Click here to learn more. *In accordance with accrediting standards for its professional education programs in law and medicine, the University does not apply religious criteria in hiring employees within those programs. All employees hired by the University, regardless of religious faith, shall be committed to Belmont’s Christ-centered, student-focused mission. Belmont's Office of Human Resources will conduct ongoing evaluations of the means by which candidates for employment are sought, to the end that the pool of candidates will include qualified women, minorities, veterans and disabled individuals. Belmont University is an equal opportunity employer under all applicable civil rights laws."
    },
