    "https://belmont.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/10/home/requisition/4792?c=belmont": {
      "title": "Office of Strategy & Innovation - Office Assistant",
      "description": "Office of Strategy & Innovation - Office Assistant | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Office of Strategy & Innovation - Office Assistant United States | req4792 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/3/2026 Back to Search Office of Strategy & Innovation - Office Assistant Employment Type Student Employee Hourly Rate $12 Special Note: All students are required to read the BU Student Employment Policy prior to submitting an application. All Federal Work-Study students should read the program rules and regulations located at http://www.belmont.edu/sfs/employment/fws.html Primary Duties and Responsibilities Job Title: Student Work-Study Assistant Department: Office of Strategy and Innovation Location: Belmont University – Office of Strategy and Innovation - Jack C. Massey, Suite 630 Hours: 10–15 hours per week (flexible around class schedule; in-person, on-site) - 3 positions available Compensation: $12/hour Position Summary The Office of Strategy and Innovation at Belmont University is seeking three dependable, professional, and detail-oriented Student Work-Study Assistants to support daily administrative operations and strategic initiatives. This role offers valuable hands-on experience in a dynamic office environment focused on innovation, collaboration, and institutional advancement. This position requires a commitment for at least the full academic semester, with the potential for extension based on performance and departmental needs. Key Responsibilities Provide general administrative support including filing, scanning, copying, and organizing documents Assist with scheduling meetings, managing calendars, and coordinating logistics Greet and welcome guests, donors, and visitors; provide front desk support and assist with check-in for meetings and appointments Run off-campus errands to procure supplies for meetings, events, and office needs Assist with preparation, assembly, and distribution of donor gifts and materials Maintain and track office inventory, including supplies and event materials; notify staff of restocking needs Prepare and format reports, presentations, and correspondence Maintain and update databases, spreadsheets, and contact lists Support planning and execution of meetings, events, and special initiatives Conduct basic research and compile information for projects as needed Perform other duties as assigned in support of the office’s strategic goals Required Qualifications Must be eligible for FWS and have been awarded. Currently enrolled student at Belmont University in good academic standing Strong organizational and time management skills Excellent interpersonal skills with a customer-service mindset Attention to detail and ability to handle confidential information Proficiency in Microsoft Office (Word, Excel, PowerPoint) or similar tools Strong written and verbal communication skills Ability to work independently and as part of a team Valid driver’s license and reliable transportation preferred for off-campus errands Work Expectations Position is in-person and on-site during scheduled hours Business casual attire is required while working in the office (guidelines can be provided upon hire) Professional demeanor is expected when interacting with guests, donors, and university staff Preferred Qualifications Interest in strategy, innovation, business, or higher education administration Previous experience in administrative support, customer service, or event coordination Familiarity with inventory tracking or data entry Required Education Must be enrolled as a student at Belmont University. Required Experience See Qualifications Apply Now Share Save Job Belmont University is a Christ-centered community. The University faculty, administration, and staff uphold Jesus as the Christ and as the measure for all things. As a community seeking to uphold Christian standards of morality, ethics, and conduct, Belmont University holds high expectations of each person who chooses to join the community. In compliance with federal law, including provisions of Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Titles VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, the Age Discrimination in Employment Act and Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973/the Americans with Disabilities Act, Belmont University does not discriminate on the basis of race, sex, color, national or ethnic origin, age, disability, military service, or sexual orientation in its administration of education policies, programs or activities; its admissions policies; or employment. Consistent with applicable civil rights law, the University primarily hires employees of the Christian faith who are committed to support the mission of the University. The University has appointed the Chief Human Resources Officer/Deputy Title IX Coordinator to serve as coordinator of non-discrimination compliance for staff and faculty. The Director of Institutional Equity and Compliance and Title IX Coordinator serves as coordinator of compliance for Title IX (sex discrimination) issues and questions for students. Click here to learn more. *In accordance with accrediting standards for its professional education programs in law and medicine, the University does not apply religious criteria in hiring employees within those programs. All employees hired by the University, regardless of religious faith, shall be committed to Belmont’s Christ-centered, student-focused mission. Belmont's Office of Human Resources will conduct ongoing evaluations of the means by which candidates for employment are sought, to the end that the pool of candidates will include qualified women, minorities, veterans and disabled individuals. Belmont University is an equal opportunity employer under all applicable civil rights laws."
    },
    "https://belmont.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/10/home/requisition/4546?c=belmont": {
      "title": "Fashion Studio - Student Worker",
      "description": "Fashion Studio - Student Worker | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Fashion Studio - Student Worker United States | req4546 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/3/2026 Back to Search Fashion Studio - Student Worker Employment Type Student Employee Hourly Rate $15 Special Note: All students are required to read the BU Student Employment Policy prior to submitting an application. All Federal Work-Study students should read the program rules and regulations located at http://www.belmont.edu/sfs/employment/fws.html Primary Duties and Responsibilities Primary Duties and Responsibilities: - Act as a studio aid by assisting students with questions in lower-level courses that includes clothing construction and patterning - Be alert to student needs and questions during open studio time - Assist faculty members in Fashion Design and Fashion Merchandising area with class preparation from cutting swatches and muslin - Oversee basic machine maintenance such as replacing threads and needles of industrial sewing machines and sergers - Keep fashion studio organized by putting away slopers and tools and upkeep of the classroom. Student must be available to work consistent days of the week/times throughout the semester, maximum of 5 hours per week . Required Qualifications Required Qualifications; - The student should be proficient at sewing on an industrial lockstitch machine and serger - The student should have strong knowledge of clothing pattern design and construction - The student should be observant, possess critical thinking skills, and have good judgement - The student must be courteous, respectful, professional, responsible, trustworthy, and able to work independently Required Education Must be enrolled as a student at Belmont University in the Fashion Department.  Must be Sophomore level or above. Required Experience Must be comfortable using and maintaining industrial sewing machines and sergers. Apply Now Share Save Job Belmont University is a Christ-centered community. The University faculty, administration, and staff uphold Jesus as the Christ and as the measure for all things. As a community seeking to uphold Christian standards of morality, ethics, and conduct, Belmont University holds high expectations of each person who chooses to join the community. In compliance with federal law, including provisions of Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Titles VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, the Age Discrimination in Employment Act and Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973/the Americans with Disabilities Act, Belmont University does not discriminate on the basis of race, sex, color, national or ethnic origin, age, disability, military service, or sexual orientation in its administration of education policies, programs or activities; its admissions policies; or employment. Consistent with applicable civil rights law, the University primarily hires employees of the Christian faith who are committed to support the mission of the University. The University has appointed the Chief Human Resources Officer/Deputy Title IX Coordinator to serve as coordinator of non-discrimination compliance for staff and faculty. The Director of Institutional Equity and Compliance and Title IX Coordinator serves as coordinator of compliance for Title IX (sex discrimination) issues and questions for students. Click here to learn more. *In accordance with accrediting standards for its professional education programs in law and medicine, the University does not apply religious criteria in hiring employees within those programs. All employees hired by the University, regardless of religious faith, shall be committed to Belmont’s Christ-centered, student-focused mission. Belmont's Office of Human Resources will conduct ongoing evaluations of the means by which candidates for employment are sought, to the end that the pool of candidates will include qualified women, minorities, veterans and disabled individuals. Belmont University is an equal opportunity employer under all applicable civil rights laws."
    },
    "https://belmont.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/10/home/requisition/4886?c=belmont": {
      "title": "Event Services - Front of House, House Manager",
      "description": "Event Services - Front of House, House Manager | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Event Services - Front of House, House Manager United States | req4886 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 7/31/2026 Back to Search Event Services - Front of House, House Manager Employment Type Student Employee Hourly Rate 18.00 Special Note: All students are required to read the BU Student Employment Policy prior to submitting an application. All Federal Work-Study students should read the program rules and regulations located at http://www.belmont.edu/sfs/employment/fws.html Primary Duties and Responsibilities The\nFront of House Team encompasses multiple positions including Usher and House\nManager. These positions operate on a flexibly scheduled basis for events\nhosted at Belmont University in the Curb Event Center arena, Fisher Center\nfor the Performing Arts, and other event spaces across campus. The House Manager positions serves as the student leader/supervisor of\nthe Front of House Usher team during events, providing direction, support, and\noversight to ensure exceptional guest service. Working alongside the Manager on\nDuty, the House Manager assists with event operations, communicating with\nushers, and addressing guest concerns as they arise. This role helps ensure\nfront-of-house operations run smoothly by enforcing venue policies, maintaining\na welcoming environment, and supporting the successful execution of each event. Required Qualifications Demonstrated reliability with strong attendance and punctuality. Working knowledge of Belmont event operations, guest service expectations, and venue procedures. Ability to remain calm and make sound decisions in fast-paced or high-pressure situations. Strong communication and interpersonal skills with the ability to interact professionally with guests, clients, and staff. Proven ability to work independently while leading and supporting a team of student employees. Experience handling customer service concerns in a professional and solution-oriented manner. Ability to follow and enforce university policies and safety procedures. Willingness to work evenings, weekends, holidays, and other event-based schedules. Required Education Must be enrolled as a student at Belmont University. Specify if the student must be a particular major or particular year in school.  No specific major. Required Experience Minimum of one (1) semester of experience as an Event Services - Front of House Usher. Apply Now Share Save Job Belmont University is a Christ-centered community. The University faculty, administration, and staff uphold Jesus as the Christ and as the measure for all things. As a community seeking to uphold Christian standards of morality, ethics, and conduct, Belmont University holds high expectations of each person who chooses to join the community. In compliance with federal law, including provisions of Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Titles VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, the Age Discrimination in Employment Act and Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973/the Americans with Disabilities Act, Belmont University does not discriminate on the basis of race, sex, color, national or ethnic origin, age, disability, military service, or sexual orientation in its administration of education policies, programs or activities; its admissions policies; or employment. Consistent with applicable civil rights law, the University primarily hires employees of the Christian faith who are committed to support the mission of the University. The University has appointed the Chief Human Resources Officer/Deputy Title IX Coordinator to serve as coordinator of non-discrimination compliance for staff and faculty. The Director of Institutional Equity and Compliance and Title IX Coordinator serves as coordinator of compliance for Title IX (sex discrimination) issues and questions for students. Click here to learn more. *In accordance with accrediting standards for its professional education programs in law and medicine, the University does not apply religious criteria in hiring employees within those programs. All employees hired by the University, regardless of religious faith, shall be committed to Belmont’s Christ-centered, student-focused mission. Belmont's Office of Human Resources will conduct ongoing evaluations of the means by which candidates for employment are sought, to the end that the pool of candidates will include qualified women, minorities, veterans and disabled individuals. Belmont University is an equal opportunity employer under all applicable civil rights laws."
    },
    "https://belmont.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/10/home/requisition/4885?c=belmont": {
      "title": "Event Services - Front of House Usher",
      "description": "Event Services - Front of House Usher | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Event Services - Front of House Usher United States | req4885 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 7/31/2026 Back to Search Event Services - Front of House Usher Employment Type Student Employee Hourly Rate 15.00 Special Note: All students are required to read the BU Student Employment Policy prior to submitting an application. All Federal Work-Study students should read the program rules and regulations located at http://www.belmont.edu/sfs/employment/fws.html Primary Duties and Responsibilities The Front of House Team encompasses multiple positions\nincluding Usher and House Manager. These positions operate on a flexibly scheduled basis for events hosted\nat Belmont University in the Curb Event Center arena, Fisher Center for\nthe Performing Arts, and other event spaces across campus. The Usher position assists in crowd management for events\nthrough duties included, but not limited to, ticket taking, assisting patrons\nin seating area, controlling access to events based on a credential\nsystem, getting guests to safety in emergency situations, acting as a general\ncustomer service representative, and helping to ensure every guest has an\nenjoyable experience while attending each event. Required Qualifications Able\nto provide great customer service. Must be able to work some nights and weekends. Friendly, personable, and a team player. Required Education Must be enrolled as a student at Belmont University. Specify if the student must be a particular major or particular year in school. Required Experience Required Experience:\nNo previous experience required.\nWillingness to learn and participate in training.\n\nPreferred Experience:\nCustomer service, hospitality, or guest relations experience.\nEvent, venue, or volunteer experience.\nExperience working with the public.\nExperience in a collaborative, team-oriented environment.\nTicket scanning experience. Apply Now Share Save Job Belmont University is a Christ-centered community. The University faculty, administration, and staff uphold Jesus as the Christ and as the measure for all things. As a community seeking to uphold Christian standards of morality, ethics, and conduct, Belmont University holds high expectations of each person who chooses to join the community. In compliance with federal law, including provisions of Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Titles VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, the Age Discrimination in Employment Act and Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973/the Americans with Disabilities Act, Belmont University does not discriminate on the basis of race, sex, color, national or ethnic origin, age, disability, military service, or sexual orientation in its administration of education policies, programs or activities; its admissions policies; or employment. Consistent with applicable civil rights law, the University primarily hires employees of the Christian faith who are committed to support the mission of the University. The University has appointed the Chief Human Resources Officer/Deputy Title IX Coordinator to serve as coordinator of non-discrimination compliance for staff and faculty. The Director of Institutional Equity and Compliance and Title IX Coordinator serves as coordinator of compliance for Title IX (sex discrimination) issues and questions for students. Click here to learn more. *In accordance with accrediting standards for its professional education programs in law and medicine, the University does not apply religious criteria in hiring employees within those programs. All employees hired by the University, regardless of religious faith, shall be committed to Belmont’s Christ-centered, student-focused mission. Belmont's Office of Human Resources will conduct ongoing evaluations of the means by which candidates for employment are sought, to the end that the pool of candidates will include qualified women, minorities, veterans and disabled individuals. Belmont University is an equal opportunity employer under all applicable civil rights laws."
    },
    "https://belmont.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/10/home/requisition/4883?c=belmont": {
      "title": "Annual Giving - Bruin Engagement Center Student Officer",
      "description": "Annual Giving - Bruin Engagement Center Student Officer | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Annual Giving - Bruin Engagement Center Student Officer United States | req4883 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 7/31/2026 Back to Search Annual Giving - Bruin Engagement Center Student Officer Employment Type Student Employee Hourly Rate $14.00 Special Note: All students are required to read the BU Student Employment Policy prior to submitting an application. All Federal Work-Study students should read the program rules and regulations located at http://www.belmont.edu/sfs/employment/fws.html Primary Duties and Responsibilities The Bruin Engagement Center is the\nhub for student philanthropy within Belmont University Advancement. As a team,\nBruin Engagement Officers engage with the Belmont community through donor\noutreach and engagement, stewardship, events, and programming. There is a major\nemphasis on digital engagement through a video messaging platform called\nThankView. Job responsibilities include: · Utilize ThankView, a personalized video\nmessaging platform, to create custom videos informing alumni and donors about\ncurrent events and fundraising opportunities at Belmont. · Content creation, digital marketing, video\nproduction and editing, graphic design and hand-crafted letters. · Help promote and execute Bruins for Life,\nBelmont's annual day of giving. · Host programs and WELL Core events that\neducate Belmont students about the importance of philanthropy. · Attend occasional donor events as\nambassadors of the university. · Support the Annual Giving team with\nadministrative tasks as needed. This position directly reports to the\nAssistant Director of Annual Giving, Avery Cooper (avery.cooper@belmont.edu). Required Qualifications Required Education Must be enrolled as a student at Belmont University. Required Experience No experience required. Apply Now Share Save Job Belmont University is a Christ-centered community. The University faculty, administration, and staff uphold Jesus as the Christ and as the measure for all things. As a community seeking to uphold Christian standards of morality, ethics, and conduct, Belmont University holds high expectations of each person who chooses to join the community. In compliance with federal law, including provisions of Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Titles VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, the Age Discrimination in Employment Act and Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973/the Americans with Disabilities Act, Belmont University does not discriminate on the basis of race, sex, color, national or ethnic origin, age, disability, military service, or sexual orientation in its administration of education policies, programs or activities; its admissions policies; or employment. Consistent with applicable civil rights law, the University primarily hires employees of the Christian faith who are committed to support the mission of the University. The University has appointed the Chief Human Resources Officer/Deputy Title IX Coordinator to serve as coordinator of non-discrimination compliance for staff and faculty. The Director of Institutional Equity and Compliance and Title IX Coordinator serves as coordinator of compliance for Title IX (sex discrimination) issues and questions for students. Click here to learn more. *In accordance with accrediting standards for its professional education programs in law and medicine, the University does not apply religious criteria in hiring employees within those programs. All employees hired by the University, regardless of religious faith, shall be committed to Belmont’s Christ-centered, student-focused mission. Belmont's Office of Human Resources will conduct ongoing evaluations of the means by which candidates for employment are sought, to the end that the pool of candidates will include qualified women, minorities, veterans and disabled individuals. Belmont University is an equal opportunity employer under all applicable civil rights laws."
