    "https://belmont.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/10/home/requisition/1711?c=belmont": {
      "title": "CEMB - Oceanway Administrative/Marketing Asst",
      "description": "CEMB - Oceanway Administrative/Marketing Asst | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) CEMB - Oceanway Administrative/Marketing Asst United States | req1711 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 7/24/2026 Back to Search CEMB - Oceanway Administrative/Marketing Asst Employment Type Student Employee Hourly Rate $12.50 Special Note: All students are required to read the BU Student Employment Policy prior to submitting an application. All Federal Work-Study students should read the program rules and regulations located at http://www.belmont.edu/sfs/employment/fws.html Primary Duties and Responsibilities This position will assist\nstaff in the areas of reception and general administration. The ideal candidate\nshould possess exceptional interpersonal skills and be able to communicate well\nwith music industry professionals, and the public at large. This position will function as the first\nimpression of Ocean Way Nashville Studios and Belmont University. Business\nprofessionalism is required at all times. Note: This is purely an\nadministrative role. Ocean Way Nashville is specifically not looking for anyone\ninterested in becoming a recording engineer, producer, or artist. Responsibilities would be,\nbut not limited to the following: Operate as general reception (answering phones) for Ocean Way Nashville Manage Access Control to clients and students entering Ocean Way Nashville Assist Ocean Way Nashville clients and staff in any requested administrative needs Organizing receipts daily for any credit card purchases at Ocean Way Nashville Closing / Weekend Shifts: Assist Client Services Representatives with any building closing procedures as needed. Required Qualifications Applicant must conduct themselves in a business professional manor as outlined by Ocean Way Nashville management Business Professional Phone Etiquette Applicant may work day, night, and weekend shifts. Required Education Must be a current Belmont Student. \nPreferred CEMB Major (Junior / Senior) Required Experience Administrative work experience in a business professional setting. Apply Now Share Save Job Belmont University is a Christ-centered community. The University faculty, administration, and staff uphold Jesus as the Christ and as the measure for all things. As a community seeking to uphold Christian standards of morality, ethics, and conduct, Belmont University holds high expectations of each person who chooses to join the community. In compliance with federal law, including provisions of Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Titles VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, the Age Discrimination in Employment Act and Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973/the Americans with Disabilities Act, Belmont University does not discriminate on the basis of race, sex, color, national or ethnic origin, age, disability, military service, or sexual orientation in its administration of education policies, programs or activities; its admissions policies; or employment. Consistent with applicable civil rights law, the University primarily hires employees of the Christian faith who are committed to support the mission of the University. The University has appointed the Chief Human Resources Officer/Deputy Title IX Coordinator to serve as coordinator of non-discrimination compliance for staff and faculty. The Director of Institutional Equity and Compliance and Title IX Coordinator serves as coordinator of compliance for Title IX (sex discrimination) issues and questions for students. Click here to learn more. *In accordance with accrediting standards for its professional education programs in law and medicine, the University does not apply religious criteria in hiring employees within those programs. All employees hired by the University, regardless of religious faith, shall be committed to Belmont’s Christ-centered, student-focused mission. Belmont's Office of Human Resources will conduct ongoing evaluations of the means by which candidates for employment are sought, to the end that the pool of candidates will include qualified women, minorities, veterans and disabled individuals. Belmont University is an equal opportunity employer under all applicable civil rights laws."
