    "https://belmont.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/10/home/requisition/4875?c=belmont": {
      "title": "Bruin Card Services – Student Worker",
      "description": "Bruin Card Services – Student Worker | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Bruin Card Services – Student Worker United States | req4875 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 7/21/2026 Back to Search Bruin Card Services – Student Worker Employment Type Student Employee Hourly Rate 12.00 Special Note: All students are required to read the BU Student Employment Policy prior to submitting an application. All Federal Work-Study students should read the program rules and regulations located at http://www.belmont.edu/sfs/employment/fws.html Primary Duties and Responsibilities This position offers an excellent opportunity to gain hands-on experience in customer service, technology support, and university operations while serving as a front-line representative for Bruin Card Services within Auxiliary Services. Student workers provide exceptional customer service to students, faculty, and staff while supporting the University's ID card program. Scheduling is flexible around class commitments; however, preference will be given to students who can work a minimum of 8 hours per week between 8:00 a.m. and 4:30 p.m., Monday through Friday. Bruin Card Services Support Serve as the first point of contact for visitors to Bruin Card Services by providing friendly, professional customer service. Guide customers through mobile credential activation and wallet setup on supported devices. Print, issue, replace, and distribute physical Bruin Cards in accordance with university policies. Assist students, faculty, and staff with questions and basic troubleshooting regarding the use of physical and mobile Bruin Cards. Verify customer identity, accurately maintain departmental records, and safeguard confidential information. Refer complex technical, access control, or policy-related questions to the Director of Bruin Card Services, Access Control, or other appropriate Auxiliary Services staff. Administrative Support Answer phones, monitor departmental email, and respond to routine customer inquiries. Assist with record keeping, data entry, and other clerical tasks. Maintain a clean, organized, and welcoming office environment. Support office projects and process improvements as assigned. Auxiliary Services Support Assist with special events, student orientations, and promotional activities. Provide support for other Auxiliary Services departments, including Dining Services, Mail Services, Bruin Bucks, Bruin Books, Vending, and the BruinShop, as departmental needs arise. Perform other duties as assigned. Required Qualifications Previous customer service, retail, help desk, or office experience. Interest in technology, mobile devices, or campus operations. Experience or interest in working with Apple and Android mobile devices. Basic proficiency with Microsoft Office (Outlook, Word, Excel, Teams). Strong attention to detail and ability to handle confidential information responsibly. Dependable, professional, and punctual. Ability to work independently while contributing to a collaborative team environment. Required Education Must be a currently enrolled Belmont University student. Required Experience Previous customer service or office experience is preferred but not required. Training will be provided. Apply Now Share Save Job Belmont University is a Christ-centered community. The University faculty, administration, and staff uphold Jesus as the Christ and as the measure for all things. As a community seeking to uphold Christian standards of morality, ethics, and conduct, Belmont University holds high expectations of each person who chooses to join the community. In compliance with federal law, including provisions of Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Titles VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, the Age Discrimination in Employment Act and Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973/the Americans with Disabilities Act, Belmont University does not discriminate on the basis of race, sex, color, national or