    "https://belmont.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/10/home/requisition/2455?c=belmont": {
      "title": "School of Pharmacy - Student Lab and Office Assistant",
      "description": "School of Pharmacy - Student Lab and Office Assistant | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) School of Pharmacy - Student Lab and Office Assistant United States | req2455 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 7/21/2026 Back to Search School of Pharmacy - Student Lab and Office Assistant Employment Type Student Employee Hourly Rate $10.00 Special Note: All students are required to read the BU Student Employment Policy prior to submitting an application. All Federal Work-Study students should read the program rules and regulations located at http://www.belmont.edu/sfs/employment/fws.html Primary Duties and Responsibilities Communicate with faculty and staff to ensure that skills laboratory and classroom activities are set up, restocked, and cleaned up in a timely manner. Conduct routine testing of eyewash/safety shower stations and equipment alarm systems. Prepare media/reagents, aliquot solutions, and handle chemicals. Move/distribute equipment, models, supplies, and glassware. May need to lift up to 25lbs. Clean laboratory benches, equipment, supplies, and glassware as needed. Collect, segregate, and/or dispose of laboratory wastes properly. Complete work assignments safely using necessary personal protective equipment and other safety devices. Perform other general laboratory and office support tasks as assigned. Copy, scan, index, and file documents. Data entry, document creation, and other computer work with Micro Office Suite. Maintenance of office, classroom, and lab inventories. Assist with special projects as needed and campus errands. Working Conditions: Adherence to laboratory safety and health policies is required, including the use of all necessary personal protective equipment. This position requires balancing, carrying, climbing, hearing with acuity, lifting, pulling, pushing, reaching ﴾both high and low﴿, repetitious finger and wrist movement, seeing near and far with depth perception and color vision, sitting, speaking clearly, standing, and walking. Required Qualifications Laboratory experience is preferred.  Lab safety training will be provided upon hire. Required Education Must be enrolled as a student at Belmont University and be a part of the Federal Work-Study Program Required Experience Laboratory experience is preferred.  Lab safety training will be provided upon hire. Apply Now Share Save Job Belmont University is a Christ-centered community. The University faculty, administration, and staff uphold Jesus as the Christ and as the measure for all things. As a community seeking to uphold Christian standards of morality, ethics, and conduct, Belmont University holds high expectations of each person who chooses to join the community. In compliance with federal law, including provisions of Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Titles VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, the Age Discrimination in Employment Act and Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973/the Americans with Disabilities Act, Belmont University does not discriminate on the basis of race, sex, color, national or ethnic origin, age, disability, military service, or sexual orientation in its administration of education policies, programs or activities; its admissions policies; or employment. Consistent with applicable civil rights law, the University primarily hires employees of the Christian faith who are committed to support the mission of the University. The University has appointed the Chief Human Resources Officer/Deputy Title IX Coordinator to serve as coordinator of non-discrimination compliance for staff and faculty. The Director of Institutional Equity and Compliance and Title IX Coordinator serves as coordinator of compliance for Title IX (sex discrimination) issues and questions for students. Click here to learn more. *In accordance with accrediting standards for its professional education programs in law and medicine, the University does not apply religious criteria in hiring employees