    "https://belmont.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/10/home/requisition/4537?c=belmont": {
      "title": "Chemistry & Physics - Student Laboratory Assistant",
      "description": "Chemistry & Physics - Student Laboratory Assistant | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Chemistry & Physics - Student Laboratory Assistant United States | req4537 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 7/16/2026 Back to Search Chemistry & Physics - Student Laboratory Assistant Employment Type Student Employee Hourly Rate $10.00 Special Note: All students are required to read the BU Student Employment Policy prior to submitting an application. All Federal Work-Study students should read the program rules and regulations located at http://www.belmont.edu/sfs/employment/fws.html Primary Duties and Responsibilities Prepare media/reagents, aliquot solutions and handle chemicals as needed., Move/distribute equipment, models, supplies, and glassware as needed., Clean laboratory benches, equipment, supplies, and glassware as needed., Communicate with faculty and staff to ensure that laboratory activities are set up, restocked, and cleaned up in a timely manner., Collect, segregate, and/or dispose of laboratory wastes properly., Complete work assignments safely using necessary personal protective equipment and other safety devices., Assist with inventory control, material safety data sheet collection, and data entry operations., Perform other general laboratory tasks as assigned. Daily duties and direct supervision will be provided by the faculty/staff member(s) responsible for specific laboratory courses.  General oversight will be provided by the Laboratory Manager for the Department of Chemistry and Physics. Prepare media/reagents, aliquot solutions and handle chemicals as needed. Function                  Move/distribute equipment, models, supplies, and glassware as needed. Clean laboratory benches, equipment, supplies, and glassware as needed Communicate with faculty and staff to ensure that laboratory activities are set up, restocked, and cleaned up in a timely manner. Collect, segregate, and/or dispose of laboratory wastes properly. Complete work assignments safely using necessary personal protective equipment and other safety devices. Assist with inventory control, material safety data sheet collection, and data entry operations. Required Qualifications Applicants must be able to complete and perform essential job functions and responsibilities as specified. Daily work assignments and direct supervision will be provided by the faculty and/or staff members responsible for specific laboratory courses. Student laboratory assistants will primarily work in teaching laboratories without continual supervision. Adherence to laboratory safety and health policies is required, including the use of all necessary personal protective equipment and other safety devices. Must have Federal Work Study to be considered. Required Education Must be currently enrolled as a Belmont University student.\nApplicants should be majoring or minoring in Chemistry or Physics.  For certain courses, such as those within the Honors or Audio Engineering Technology programs, applicants with other majors or minors will be considered if they are currently enrolled in the course or have taken the course. Required Experience Applicants must be currently enrolled in laboratory courses or must have taken laboratory courses within the College of Sciences and Mathematics. Apply Now Share Save Job Belmont University is a Christ-centered community. The University faculty, administration, and staff uphold Jesus as the Christ and as the measure for all things. As a community seeking to uphold Christian standards of morality, ethics, and conduct, Belmont University holds high expectations of each person who chooses to join the community. In compliance with federal law, including provisions of Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Titles VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, the Age Discrimination in Employment Act and Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973/the Americans with Disabilities Act, Belmont University does not discriminate on the basis of race, sex, color, national or ethnic origin, age, disability, military service, or sexual orientation in its administration of education policies, programs or activities; its admissions policies; or employment. Consistent with applicable civil rights law, the University primarily hires employees of the Christian faith who are committed to support the mission of the University. The University has appointed the Chief Human Resources Officer/Deputy Title IX Coordinator to serve as coordinator of non-discrimination compliance for staff and faculty. The Director of Institutional Equity and Compliance and Title IX Coordinator serves as coordinator of compliance for Title IX (sex discrimination) issues and questions for students. Click here to learn more. *In accordance with accrediting standards for its professional education programs in law and medicine, the University does not apply religious criteria in hiring employees within those programs. All employees hired by the University, regardless of religious faith, shall be committed to Belmont’s Christ-centered, student-focused mission. Belmont's Office of Human Resources will conduct ongoing evaluations of the means by which candidates for employment are sought, to the end that the pool of candidates will include qualified women, minorities, veterans and disabled individuals. Belmont University is an equal opportunity employer under all applicable civil rights laws."
