    "https://belmont.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/10/home/requisition/4854?c=belmont": {
      "title": "The Store (Centennial Location) - Operations Assistant",
      "description": "The Store (Centennial Location) - Operations Assistant | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) The Store (Centennial Location) - Operations Assistant United States | req4854 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 6/30/2026 Back to Search The Store (Centennial Location) - Operations Assistant Employment Type Student Employee Hourly Rate $15 Special Note: All students are required to read the BU Student Employment Policy prior to submitting an application. All Federal Work-Study students should read the program rules and regulations located at http://www.belmont.edu/sfs/employment/fws.html Primary Duties and Responsibilities Please note this a Saturday only position at our Centennial Location (2303 Patterson Street Nashville, TN 37203) . Assist on Saturday, the Operations Manager, in partnership with the Operations Director to ensure the smooth operations of The Store, the distribution of food to customers, maintaining The Store's cleanliness, restock and proper storage of food, in a manner consistent with The Store’s values of dignity and choice. Vendor Deliveries: Meets vendors delivering food and supplies and assist in loading supplies into appropriate storage location (refrigerator, shelves, etc.).  as needed. Volunteer Training: Work with volunteer coordinator to ensure volunteers are oriented to their job and know how to complete assigned tasks. Volunteer Assistance: Help oversee volunteers in all aspects of The Store operations during restocking, inventory, and shopping hours, providing assistance and direction when needed.  May serve as point of contact for the volunteer shift leader and other volunteers. Customer Service:  Assist customers as needed during shopping to ensure a positive shopping experience. Restocking: Work with volunteers throughout shopping hours to ensure shelves are restocked as needed. Inventory: May need to take inventory of food and non-food items as necessary to inform future ordering/restocking. Other duties as assigned. Working conditions: - Ability to lift a minimum of 60 lbs. - Stand for long periods - Highly physical position Required Qualifications Applicant must have FWS Award to apply. Excellent customer service skills. Relevant training or certification in food safety.  (Not required, but helpful) Valid driver’s license. (Not required, but helpful) Required Education Must be enrolled as a student at Belmont University. Required Experience No experience required. Apply Now Share Save Job Belmont University is a Christ-centered community. The University faculty, administration, and staff uphold Jesus as the Christ and as the measure for all things. As a community seeking to uphold Christian standards of morality, ethics, and conduct, Belmont University holds high expectations of each person who chooses to join the community. In compliance with federal law, including provisions of Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Titles VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, the Age Discrimination in Employment Act and Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973/the Americans with Disabilities Act, Belmont University does not discriminate on the basis of race, sex, color, national or ethnic origin, age, disability, military service, or sexual orientation in its administration of education policies, programs or activities; its admissions policies; or employment. Consistent with applicable civil rights law, the University primarily hires employees of the Christian faith who are committed to support the mission of the University. The University has appointed the Chief Human Resources Officer/Deputy Title IX Coordinator to serve as coordinator of non-discrimination compliance for staff and faculty. The Director of Institutional Equity and Compliance and Title IX Coordinator serves as coordinator of compliance for Title IX (sex discrimination) issues and questions for students. Click here to learn more. *In accordance with accrediting standards for its professional education programs in law and medicine, the University does not apply religious criteria in hiring employees within those programs. All employees hired by the University, regardless of religious faith, shall be committed to Belmont’s Christ-centered, student-focused mission. Belmont's Office of Human Resources will conduct ongoing evaluations of the means by which candidates for employment are sought, to the end that the pool of candidates will include qualified women, minorities, veterans and disabled individuals. Belmont University is an equal opportunity employer under all applicable civil rights laws."
