    "https://belmont.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/10/home/requisition/2425?c=belmont": {
      "title": "FitRec - Beaman Trainer I",
      "description": "FitRec - Beaman Trainer I | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) FitRec - Beaman Trainer I United States | req2425 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 7/21/2025 Back to Search FitRec - Beaman Trainer I Employment Type Student Employee Hourly Rate $12.75 Special Note: All students are required to read the BU Student Employment Policy prior to submitting an application. All Federal Work-Study students should read the program rules and regulations located at http://www.belmont.edu/sfs/employment/fws.html Primary Duties and Responsibilities Beaman Trainer 1 is transitional position for Jumpstart Trainers who have completed their in-house certification but have not yet attained a national certification. Beaman Trainer 1 provide members of the Belmont community with personal training and wellness education services. Duties Include: Safely and effectively take training clients through workouts using proper form and spotting techniques; Facilitate wellness education programming for members of the Belmont community; Maintain accurate training records, including but not limited to client session notes and training logs; Educate clients on the proper use of cardiovascular and strength equipment; Develop a positive relationship between the trainer and the client; Attend Reunions, CEUs, trainings and other developmental programs; Other duties assigned The physical requirements described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. While performing the duties of this job, the employee’s vision must be adequate to read correspondence, computer screen, forms, etc. The employee is regularly required to talk and hear. The employee frequently is required to stand; walk; use hands to finger, handle or feel; and reach with hands and arms. This position is very active and requires standing, walking, bending, kneeling, stooping, crouching, crawling and climbing all day. The employee must frequently lift and move loads of 20-50 pounds. Close vision, distance vision, peripheral vision, depth perception and the ability to adjust focus, with or without corrective lenses. Required Qualifications Excellent oral communication skills with co-workers, supervisors, patrons and guests; Excellent customer interaction skills with co-workers, supervisors, patrons and guests; Ability to work outside conventional work hours (e.g. weekends, late nights and some holidays); Strong organizational skills; Must have a basic knowledge of fitness programming including proper form, client interaction, and exercise prescription Required Education Must be enrolled as a current student at Belmont University. Required Experience Completion of in-house certification course and Beaman Basics package. Apply Now Share Save Job Belmont University is a Christ-centered community. The University faculty, administration, and staff uphold Jesus as the Christ and as the measure for all things. As a community seeking to uphold Christian standards of morality, ethics, and conduct, Belmont University holds high expectations of each person who chooses to join the community. In compliance with federal law, including provisions of Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Titles VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, the Age Discrimination in Employment Act and Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973/the Americans with Disabilities Act, Belmont University does not discriminate on the basis of race, sex, color, national or ethnic origin, age, disability, military service, or sexual orientation in its administration of education policies, programs or activities; its admissions policies; or employment. Consistent with applicable civil rights law, the University primarily hires employees of the Christian faith who are committed to support the mission of the Un