    "https://belmont.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/10/home/requisition/2424?c=belmont": {
      "title": "FitRec - Group Fitness Instructor III",
      "description": "FitRec - Group Fitness Instructor III | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) FitRec - Group Fitness Instructor III United States | req2424 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 7/21/2025 Back to Search FitRec - Group Fitness Instructor III Employment Type Student Employee Hourly Rate $20.75 Special Note: All students are required to read the BU Student Employment Policy prior to submitting an application. All Federal Work-Study students should read the program rules and regulations located at http://www.belmont.edu/sfs/employment/fws.html Primary Duties and Responsibilities Group Fitness Instructor 3 is a position for nationally certified trainers who hold an advanced NCCA-accredited certification or an undergraduate degree. Group Fitness Instructor 3 provide the Belmont community with group fitness instruction and wellness education services. Duties Include: Safely and effectively conduct group fitness classes for the Belmont community using proper form, cueing techniques, and appropriate regressions and progressions; Maintain and manage records regarding class registration and attendance; Facilitate wellness education programming for members of the Belmont community; Develop and maintain a positive and supportive atmosphere for class participants; Attend Reunions, CEUs, trainings and developmental programs; Other duties as assigned The physical requirements described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. While performing the duties of this job, the employee’s vision must be adequate to read correspondence, computer screen, forms, etc. The employee is regularly required to talk and hear. The employee frequently is required to stand; walk; use hands to finger, handle or feel; and reach with hands and arms. This position is very active and requires standing, walking, bending, kneeling, stooping, crouching, crawling and climbing all day. The employee must frequently lift and move loads of 20-50 pounds. Close vision, distance vision, peripheral vision, depth perception and the ability to adjust focus, with or without corrective lenses. Required Qualifications Excellent oral communication skills with co-workers, supervisors, patrons and guests; Excellent customer interaction skills with co-workers, supervisors, patrons and guests; Ability to work outside conventional work hours (e.g. weekends, late nights and some holidays); Must have a knowledge of fitness programming including proper form, participant interaction, and exercise prescription; Must possess the ability to design and implement evidence-backed exercise classes that satisfy participant needs while remaining within the scope of practice as stated by their certifying organization; Ability to effectively progress and regress exercises based on participant fitness levels Required Education Must be enrolled as a current student at Belmont University. Required Experience Current NCCA-accredited advanced fitness or specialty certification (i.e. SPIN, ZUMBA, Barre, Yoga) or an undergraduate degree. Apply Now Share Save Job Belmont University is a Christ-centered community. The University faculty, administration, and staff uphold Jesus as the Christ and as the measure for all things. As a community seeking to uphold Christian standards of morality, ethics, and conduct, Belmont University holds high expectations of each person who chooses to join the community. In compliance with federal law, including provisions of Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Titles VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, the Age Discrimination in Employment Act and Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973/the Americans with Disabilities Act, Belmont University does not discriminate on the basis of race, sex, color, national or ethnic origin, age, disability, military service, or sexual orientation in its administration of education policies, programs or activities; its admissions policies; or employment. Consistent with applicable civil rights law, the University primarily hires employees of the Christian faith who are committed to support the mission of the University. The University has appointed the Chief Human Resources Officer/Deputy Title IX Coordinator to serve as coordinator of non-discrimination compliance for staff and faculty. The Director of Institutional Equity and Compliance and Title IX Coordinator serves as coordinator of compliance for Title IX (sex discrimination) issues and questions for students. Click here to learn more. *In accordance with accrediting standards for its professional education programs in law and medicine, the University does not apply religious criteria in hiring employees within those programs. All employees hired by the University, regardless of religious faith, shall be committed to Belmont’s Christ-centered, student-focused mission. Belmont's Office of Human Resources will conduct ongoing evaluations of the means by which candidates for employment are sought, to the end that the pool of candidates will include qualified women, minorities, veterans and disabled individuals. Belmont University is an equal opportunity employer under all applicable civil rights laws."
    },
