    "https://belmont.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/10/home/requisition/2420?c=belmont": {
      "title": "FitRec - Beaman Trainer III",
      "description": "FitRec - Beaman Trainer III | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) FitRec - Beaman Trainer III United States | req2420 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 7/21/2025 Back to Search FitRec - Beaman Trainer III Employment Type Student Employee Hourly Rate $20.75 Special Note: All students are required to read the BU Student Employment Policy prior to submitting an application. All Federal Work-Study students should read the program rules and regulations located at http://www.belmont.edu/sfs/employment/fws.html Primary Duties and Responsibilities Beaman Trainer 3 is a position for nationally\ncertified trainers who hold an advanced NCCA-accredited certification or an\nundergraduate degree. Beaman Trainer 3 provide the Belmont community with\npersonal training and wellness education services. Duties Include: Safely and effectively\ntake personal training clients through workouts using proper form and spotting\ntechniques Facilitate wellness education programming for members of the\nBelmont community Maintain accurate training records, including but not\nlimited to client session notes and training logs Educate clients on the\nproper use of cardiovascular and strength equipment Develop a positive\nrelationship between the trainer and the client Attend Reunions, CEUs, training\nand other developmental programs Other duties assigned The physical requirements\ndescribed here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to\nsuccessfully perform the essential functions of this job. Reasonable\naccommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform essential\nfunctions. While performing the duties of this job, the employee’s vision must\nbe adequate to read correspondence, computer screen, forms, etc. The employee\nis regularly required to talk and hear. The employee frequently is required to\nstand; walk; use hands to finger, handle or feel; and reach with hands and\narms. This position is very active and r