    "https://belmont.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/10/home/requisition/4112?c=belmont": {
      "title": "Maintenance Tech II",
      "description": "Maintenance Tech II | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Maintenance Tech II United States | req4112 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 7/30/2024 Back to Search Maintenance Tech II We are now accepting applications for a qualified Maintenance Tech II at Belmont University. Employment Type Staff Internal Job Category Non-Exempt (Staff) Full-Time Department Maintenance Services Hours 40 Primary Duties and Responsibilities: To provide basic daily maintenance for University buildings and equipment. Performs basic maintenance/repairs in all fields. Includes electrical, HVAC, plumbing, and carpentry repairs involving bulb replacement, switch/outlet repair, filter replacement, unclogging plumbing fixtures, repairs to doors, windows, and roofs. Interprets scope of work assigned, time involved, materials needed, orders and picks up materials. Performs clean up and material return from job location, maintains tools used and returns tools to shop at end of each day. Interprets basic mechanical meters and properly operates electrical machinery within crafts. Involves operation and understanding of volt/ohm meters, thermostats, thermometers, pressure gauges, plumbing cables, table saws, drill press and etc. Performs preventative maintenance inspections, makes necessary repairs, and completes paperwork of such preventative maintenance in a timely manner. Assist in emergency and after hour repairs as needed. The above statements describe the job’s essential responsibilities and requirements. They are not an exhaustive list of the duties that may be assigned to job incumbents. Required Qualifications : Belmont University seeks to attract and retain highly qualified faculty and staff who will support our mission and vision. As a Christ-centered and student-focused community, we aim to: Form diverse leaders of character; Equip people to solve the world’s complex problems through teaching, research and service; And be radical champions for helping people and communities flourish. Must have a valid driver's license and will be required to drive for Belmont business. Basic knowledge of the methods, materials, tools, and practices of building maintenance. Basic knowledge of the occupational hazards and safety precautions of the trades involved. Skill in the care and use of the tools and equipment used in the trades involved. Ability to detect defects in equipment and to make proper repairs or adjustments. Ability to supervise a group of semi or non-skilled workers. Ability to work from pencil sketches and diagrams. Must supply his/her own hand tools. Demonstrate the ability to read and write in order to follow written instruction. Demonstrate the ability to work with hands and work in mechanically oriented situations following instructions of the maintenance manager. Basic knowledge of electrical, HVAC, plumbing and carpentry required. Required Education High school diploma or equivalent. Required Experience Three years minimum experience in a maintenance or equivalent trade. The selected candidate will be required to complete a background check satisfactory to the University. Belmont University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Apply Now Share Save Job Belmont University is a Christ-centered community. The University faculty, administration, and staff uphold Jesus as the Christ and as the measure for all things. As a community seeking to uphold Christian standards of morality, ethics, and conduct, Belmont University holds high expectations of each person who chooses to join the community. In compliance with federal law, including provisions of Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Titles VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, the Age Discrimination in Employment Act and Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973/the Americans with Disabilities Act, Belmont University does not discriminate on the basis of race, sex, color, national or ethnic origin, age, disability, military service, or sexual orientation in its administration of education policies, programs or activities; its admissions policies; or employment. Consistent with applicable civil rights law, the University primarily hires employees of the Christian faith who are committed to support the mission of the University. The University has appointed the Chief Human Resources Officer/Deputy Title IX Coordinator to serve as coordinator of non-discrimination compliance for staff and faculty. The Director of Institutional Equity and Compliance and Title IX Coordinator serves as coordinator of compliance for Title IX (sex discrimination) issues and questions for students. Click here to learn more. *In accordance with accrediting standards for its professional education programs in law and medicine, the University does not apply religious criteria in hiring employees within those programs. All employees hired by the University, regardless of religious faith, shall be committed to Belmont’s Christ-centered, student-focused mission. Belmont's Office of Human Resources will conduct ongoing evaluations of the means by which candidates for employment are sought, to the end that the pool of candidates will include qualified women, minorities, veterans and disabled individuals. Belmont University is an equal opportunity employer under all applicable civil rights laws."
