    "https://belmont.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/10/home/requisition/227?c=belmont": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant (Temporary Pool)",
      "description": "Administrative Assistant (Temporary Pool) | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Administrative Assistant (Temporary Pool) United States | req227 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 6/3/2024 Back to Search Administrative Assistant (Temporary Pool) We are now accepting qualified applicants for our Administrative Assistant temporary pool. Employment Type Temporary Internal Job Category Non-Exempt (Staff) Department Varies Primary Duties and Responsibilities: This is a short-term, temporary administrative assistant role working for various departments at Belmont University. Placement depends on need. Job functions will vary according to need, but basic expectations include: Answer multiple incoming telephone lines. Take and route messages when appropriate. Make appointments for customers. Manage calendars for office personnel. Greet and assist customers as they enter the office. Perform general clerical functions for the office. Maintain a clean, professional front office. The above statements describe the job's essential responsibilities. They are not an exhaustive list of the duties that may be assigned. Serve as temporary administrative assistant as assigned for various departments at Belmont University. Serve as temporary administrative assistant as assigned for various departments at Belmont University. Serve as temporary administrative assistant as assigned for various departments at Belmont University. Required Qualifications : Belmont University seeks to attract and retain highly qualified faculty and staff that share the University's values and will contribute to its mission and vision to be a leader among teaching universities bringing together the best of liberal arts and professional education in a Christian community of learning and service. Knowledge of basic computer functions including Microsoft Word and Excel. Ability to manage multiple incoming phone lines and voicemail. Ability to deal with several customers simultaneously and prioritize needs as necessary. Eagerness to assist internal and/or external customers with a professional and courteous attitude. Ability to work in a team environment with diverse constituents. Professional mannerism and appearance. Ability to thrive in a fast-paced environment. Required Education High school diploma or GED required. Some college-level coursework preferred. Required Experience 0-2 years office or customer service experience. Computer skills require basic MS Office and internet use. The selected candidate will be required to complete a background check satisfactory to the University. Belmont University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Apply Now Share Save Job Belmont University is a Christ-centered community. The University faculty, administration, and staff uphold Jesus as the Christ and as the measure for all things. As a community seeking to uphold Christian standards of morality, ethics, and conduct, Belmont University holds high expectations of each person who chooses to join the community. In compliance with federal law, including provisions of Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Titles VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, the Age Discrimination in Employment Act and Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973/the Americans with Disabilities Act, Belmont University does not discriminate on the basis of race, sex, color, national or ethnic origin, age, disability, military service, or sexual orientation in its administration of education policies, programs or activities; its admissions policies; or employment. Consistent with applicable civil rights law, the University primarily hires employees of the Christian faith who are committed to support the mission of the University. The University has appointed the Chief Human Resources Officer/Deputy Title IX Coordinator to serve as coordinator of non-discrimination compliance for staff and faculty. The Director of Institutional Equity and Compliance and Title IX Coordinator serves as coordinator of compliance for Title IX (sex discrimination) issues and questions for students. Click here to learn more. *In accordance with accrediting standards for its professional education programs in law and medicine, the University does not apply religious criteria in hiring employees within those programs. All employees hired by the University, regardless of religious faith, shall be committed to Belmont’s Christ-centered, student-focused mission. Belmont's Office of Human Resources will conduct ongoing evaluations of the means by which candidates for employment are sought, to the end that the pool of candidates will include qualified women, minorities, veterans and disabled individuals. Belmont University is an equal opportunity employer under all applicable civil rights laws."
