    "https://belmont.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/10/home/requisition/4989?c=belmont": {
      "title": "Admissions Coordinator for the Massey College of Business",
      "description": "Admissions Coordinator for the Massey College of Business | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Admissions Coordinator for the Massey College of Business United States | req4989 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/22/2026 Back to Search Admissions Coordinator for the Massey College of Business We are now accepting applications for a qualified Admissions Coordinator for the Massey College of Business at Belmont University. Employment Type Staff Internal Job Category Exempt (Staff) Full-Time Department Ofc VP for Enrollment Hours 37.5 Primary Duties and Responsibilities: This position involves overseeing admissions counseling,\nrecruitment, and general office tasks for a diverse range of applicants for a\nspecific college. The objective is to manage the enrollment process for various\nstudent categories, including undergraduate transfers, re-enrolling students,\nfreshmen, and second-degree program candidates. The role requires maintaining a\ndeep understanding of Belmont University's vision and collaborating with\nadmissions counselors, faculty, and various teams to enhance recruitment\nstrategies, coordinate events, and manage the virtual presence of the specific\ncollege and/or population through the website and social media platforms.\nAdditionally, the position involves reporting on recruitment progress,\nparticipating in process improvement teams, and contributing to marketing\ninitiatives for prospective students. Recruit\n     undergraduate prospective students for a specific academic college.\n     Maintain a breadth and depth of knowledge of Belmont's unique\n     opportunities to effectively communicate the academic offerings of their\n     college and Belmont's social and spiritual composition to external\n     stakeholders.  Plan and execute local and regional high school\n     student outreach and attend industry conferences and college fairs when\n     applicable to promote programs. Serve\n     as academic and scholarship (if applicable) liaison between Admissions and\n     designated college by maintaining Dean and faculty relations, attending\n     college meetings and events, and representing Admissions at college\n     events. Facilitate\n     daily and virtual college information sessions for prospective families.\n     Partner with Admissions visit team for enhanced daily visit, graduate\n     information sessions, and Saturday visit day programming. Work\n     alongside University Marketing to execute the college's marketing plan\n     including the creation of marketing pieces, promotional items, website\n     management, and prospect, alumni and parent outreach, and content for\n     social media channels (including but not limited to CampusESP, Instagram,\n     Facebook, and LinkedIn). Utilize\n     enrollment and university CRMs to analyze data related to the applicant\n     pool and identify trends, demographics, and other patterns to make\n     informed decisions about admissions strategies, targets and departmental\n     scholarships (if applicable). Other\n     duties as assigned. Required Qualifications : Belmont University seeks to attract and retain highly qualified faculty and staff who will support our mission and vision. As a Christ-centered and student-focused community, we aim to: Form diverse leaders of character; Equip people to solve the world’s complex problems through teaching, research and service; And be radical champions for helping people and communities flourish. Bachelor’s degree required. Previous private college\nexperience as a student or employee preferred. Experience in the academic\nsubject area of the college is preferred. Must possess a current valid driver's\nlicense with good driving record. Required Education Bachelor’s degree Required Experience Previous private college experience as a student or employee preferred. Experience in the academic subject area of the college is preferred. The selected candidate will be required to complete a background check satisfactory to the University. Belmont University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Apply Now Share Save Job Belmont University is a Christ-centered community. The University faculty, administration, and staff uphold Jesus as the Christ and as the measure for all things. As a community seeking to uphold Christian standards of morality, ethics, and conduct, Belmont University holds high expectations of each person who chooses to join the community. In compliance with federal law, including provisions of Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Titles VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, the Age Discrimination in Employment Act and Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973/the Americans with Disabilities Act, Belmont University does not discriminate on the basis of race, sex, color, national or ethnic origin, age, disability, military service, or sexual orientation in its administration of education policies, programs or activities; its admissions policies; or employment. Consistent with applicable civil rights law, the University primarily hires employees of the Christian faith who are committed to support the mission of the University. The University has appointed the Chief Human Resources Officer/Deputy Title IX Coordinator to serve as coordinator of non-discrimination compliance for staff and faculty. The Director of Institutional Equity and Compliance and Title IX Coordinator serves as coordinator of compliance for Title IX (sex discrimination) issues and questions for students. Click here to learn more. *In accordance with accrediting standards for its professional education programs in law and medicine, the University does not apply religious criteria in hiring employees within those programs. All employees hired by the University, regardless of religious faith, shall be committed to Belmont’s Christ-centered, student-focused mission. Belmont's Office of Human Resources will conduct ongoing evaluations of the means by which candidates for employment are sought, to the end that the pool of candidates will include qualified women, minorities, veterans and disabled individuals. Belmont University is an equal opportunity employer under all applicable civil rights laws."
